1
00:00:49,189 --> 00:00:52,523
<i>-Is everything in place?
- You weren't supposed to relieve me.</i>

2
00:00:52,734 --> 00:00:55,442
<i>I know, but I felt like taking a shift.</i>

3
00:00:55,904 --> 00:00:58,362
<i>You like him, don't you?
You like watching him.</i>

4
00:00:58,574 --> 00:01:01,692
- <i>Don't be ridiculous.</i>
- We're <i>gonna kill him. You understand?</i>

5
00:01:01,868 --> 00:01:04,360
<i>Morpheus believes he is the One.</i>

6
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:07,538
<i>-Do you?
- It doesn't matter what I believe.</i>

7
00:01:07,749 --> 00:01:09,365
<i>You don't, do you?</i>

8
00:01:09,585 --> 00:01:11,747
<i>-Did you hear that?
- Hear what?</i>

9
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:13,627
<i>Are you sure this line is clean?</i>

10
00:01:13,839 --> 00:01:15,796
<i>Yeah, of course I'm sure.</i>

11
00:01:16,174 --> 00:01:17,585
<i>I better go.</i>

12
00:01:55,422 --> 00:01:57,333
- Freeze! Police!
- Hands on your head!

13
00:01:57,758 --> 00:01:58,998
Do it! Do it now!

14
00:02:20,405 --> 00:02:23,022
- Lieutenant.
- Oh, shit.

15
00:02:23,867 --> 00:02:27,030
Lieutenant, you were given
specific orders.

16
00:02:27,245 --> 00:02:29,031
Hey, I'm just doing my job.

17
00:02:29,623 --> 00:02:34,083
You give me that "juris-my-dick-tion"
crap, you can cram it up your ass.

18
00:02:34,544 --> 00:02:37,036
The orders were for your protection.

19
00:02:38,548 --> 00:02:40,710
I think we can handle one little girl.

20
00:02:45,847 --> 00:02:47,633
I sent two units!

21
00:02:47,849 --> 00:02:49,431
They're bringing her down now!

22
00:02:49,643 --> 00:02:52,761
No, Lieutenant, your men are
already dead.

23
00:03:21,967 --> 00:03:22,957
Shit.

24
00:03:25,846 --> 00:03:27,962
Morpheus, the line was traced.
I don't know how.

25
00:03:28,140 --> 00:03:29,801
<i>I know. They cut the hard line.</i>

26
00:03:30,016 --> 00:03:32,257
<i>There's no time.
Get to another exit.</i>

27
00:03:32,477 --> 00:03:34,889
- Are there any agents?
- <i>Yes.</i>

28
00:03:35,105 --> 00:03:36,311
Goddamn it.

29
00:03:36,523 --> 00:03:38,105
<i>You have to focus, Trinity.</i>

30
00:03:38,316 --> 00:03:40,683
<i>There's a phone at Wells and Lake.</i>

31
00:03:41,111 --> 00:03:42,772
<i>You can make it.</i>

32
00:03:42,988 --> 00:03:44,604
- All right.
- <i>Go.</i>

33
00:04:46,676 --> 00:04:47,882
That's impossible.

34
00:05:22,796 --> 00:05:24,833
Get up, Trinity.
Just get up.

35
00:05:25,465 --> 00:05:26,705
Get up.

36
00:05:26,705 --> 00:05:36,705
<b>Subtitle | www.movieddl.me</b>

37
00:06:12,596 --> 00:06:14,086
She got out.

38
00:06:14,431 --> 00:06:15,717
It doesn't matter.

39
00:06:15,932 --> 00:06:18,014
The informant is real.

40
00:06:19,227 --> 00:06:22,936
- We have the name of their next target.
- The name is Neo.

41
00:06:26,192 --> 00:06:27,728
We'll need a search running.

42
00:06:28,028 --> 00:06:29,985
It has already begun.

43
00:07:24,709 --> 00:07:25,915
What?

44
00:07:31,716 --> 00:07:33,172
What the hell?

45
00:07:40,850 --> 00:07:42,761
"Follow the white rabbit."

46
00:07:54,572 --> 00:07:55,812
Who is it?

47
00:07:55,991 --> 00:07:57,356
It's Choi.

48
00:08:10,797 --> 00:08:12,037
You're two hours late.

49
00:08:12,590 --> 00:08:15,582
- I know. It's her fault.
- You got the money?

50
00:08:17,637 --> 00:08:18,877
Two grand.

51
00:08:19,639 --> 00:08:20,879
Hold on.

52
00:08:38,575 --> 00:08:39,940
Hallelujah.

53
00:08:40,243 --> 00:08:43,110
You're my savior, man.
My own personal Jesus Christ.

54
00:08:43,288 --> 00:08:44,870
You get caught using that...

55
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:47,577
I know. This never happened.
You don't exist.

56
00:08:48,710 --> 00:08:50,792
- Right.
- Something wrong, man?

57
00:08:51,004 --> 00:08:53,041
You look a little whiter than usual.

58
00:08:54,174 --> 00:08:56,336
My computer, it...

59
00:08:59,345 --> 00:09:04,636
You ever have that feeling where you're
not sure if you're awake or still dreaming?

60
00:09:04,809 --> 00:09:07,471
All the time.
It's called mescaline.

61
00:09:07,979 --> 00:09:10,095
It's the only way to fly.

62
00:09:10,356 --> 00:09:14,065
Hey, look, it just sounds like
you might need to unplug, man.

63
00:09:14,235 --> 00:09:16,226
You know? Get some R and R?

64
00:09:16,654 --> 00:09:20,363
What do you think, Dujour?
Should we take him with us?

65
00:09:22,368 --> 00:09:23,654
Definitely.

66
00:09:23,870 --> 00:09:26,953
No, I can't. I have work tomorrow.

67
00:09:27,499 --> 00:09:28,739
Come on.

68
00:09:28,958 --> 00:09:31,575
It'll be fun. I promise.

69
00:09:38,093 --> 00:09:39,583
Yeah.

70
00:09:40,470 --> 00:09:42,256
Sure. I'll go.

71
00:10:09,999 --> 00:10:11,660
Hello, Neo.

72
00:10:12,460 --> 00:10:13,996
How do you know that name?

73
00:10:14,212 --> 00:10:15,998
I know a lot about you.

74
00:10:16,881 --> 00:10:18,997
- Who are you?
- My name is Trinity.

75
00:10:19,884 --> 00:10:21,124
Trinity.

76
00:10:22,887 --> 00:10:26,130
The Trinity?
That cracked the IRS D-base?

77
00:10:26,349 --> 00:10:27,839
That was a long time ago.

78
00:10:28,059 --> 00:10:29,925
- Jesus.
- What?

79
00:10:30,436 --> 00:10:32,177
I just thought...

80
00:10:34,023 --> 00:10:36,890
- ...you were a guy.
- Most guys do.

81
00:10:38,069 --> 00:10:40,276
That was you on my computer.

82
00:10:40,905 --> 00:10:45,365
- How did you do that?
- Right now, all I can tell you...

83
00:10:45,952 --> 00:10:47,534
...is that you're in danger.

84
00:10:47,954 --> 00:10:50,412
- I brought you here to warn you.
- Of what?

85
00:10:50,957 --> 00:10:52,698
They're watching you, Neo.

86
00:10:53,418 --> 00:10:55,659
- Who is?
- Please, just listen.

87
00:10:59,174 --> 00:11:01,040
I know why you're here, Neo.

88
00:11:01,801 --> 00:11:03,792
I know what you've been doing.

89
00:11:04,053 --> 00:11:05,885
I know why you hardly sleep...

90
00:11:06,222 --> 00:11:09,340
...why you live alone, and why,
night after night...

91
00:11:09,559 --> 00:11:11,891
...you sit at your computer.

92
00:11:13,062 --> 00:11:14,598
You're looking for him.

93
00:11:15,356 --> 00:11:18,394
I know, because I was once
looking for the same thing.

94
00:11:18,943 --> 00:11:21,025
And when he found me...

95
00:11:21,654 --> 00:11:24,692
...he told me I wasn't really
looking for him...

96
00:11:25,658 --> 00:11:27,399
... I was looking for an answer.

97
00:11:28,036 --> 00:11:31,154
It's the question that drives us, Neo.

98
00:11:31,789 --> 00:11:34,497
It's the question
that brought you here.

99
00:11:36,628 --> 00:11:37,959
You know the question...

100
00:11:38,254 --> 00:11:39,710
...just as I did.

101
00:11:41,257 --> 00:11:42,918
What is the Matrix?

102
00:11:43,134 --> 00:11:45,592
The answer is out there, Neo.

103
00:11:46,262 --> 00:11:48,219
It's looking for you.

104
00:11:49,098 --> 00:11:50,714
And it will find you...

105
00:11:51,017 --> 00:11:53,008
...if you want it to.

106
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:00,731
Shit.

107
00:12:00,902 --> 00:12:02,108
Shit, shit.

108
00:12:12,372 --> 00:12:15,285
You have a problem with authority,
Mr. Anderson.

109
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:19,494
You believe that you are special,
that somehow the rules do not apply to you.

110
00:12:20,255 --> 00:12:22,292
Obviously, you are mistaken.

111
00:12:25,134 --> 00:12:28,092
This is one of the top
software companies in the world. <i>..</i>

112
00:12:28,346 --> 00:12:31,759
...because every employee understands
they are part of a whole.

113
00:12:31,975 --> 00:12:36,560
Thus, if an employee has a problem,
the company has a problem.

114
00:12:38,856 --> 00:12:42,065
The time has come to make
a choice, Mr. Anderson.

115
00:12:42,986 --> 00:12:46,820
Either you choose to be at your desk
on time from this day forth...

116
00:12:47,490 --> 00:12:49,982
...or you choose to find yourself
another job.

117
00:12:50,910 --> 00:12:52,275
Do I make myself clear?

118
00:12:52,495 --> 00:12:54,657
Yes, Mr. Rhineheart.
Perfectly clear.

119
00:13:03,381 --> 00:13:04,963
Thomas Anderson?

120
00:13:06,509 --> 00:13:07,920
Yeah, that's me.

121
00:13:15,893 --> 00:13:17,099
Great.

122
00:13:18,479 --> 00:13:19,685
Have a nice day.

123
00:13:35,538 --> 00:13:37,529
- Hello?
- <i>Hello, Neo.</i>

124
00:13:37,707 --> 00:13:39,789
<i>Do you know who this is?</i>

125
00:13:42,086 --> 00:13:43,872
- Morpheus.
- <i>Yes.</i>

126
00:13:44,088 --> 00:13:46,079
<i>I've been looking for you, Neo.</i>

127
00:13:46,299 --> 00:13:49,542
<i>I don't know if you're ready to see
what I want to show you...</i>

128
00:13:49,761 --> 00:13:52,970
<i>...but, unfortunately, you and I
have run out of time.</i>

129
00:13:53,181 --> 00:13:56,924
<i>They're coming for you, Neo,
and I don't know what they're going to do.</i>

130
00:13:57,143 --> 00:13:58,508
Who's coming for me?

131
00:13:58,728 --> 00:14:00,844
<i>Stand up and see for yourself.</i>

132
00:14:01,064 --> 00:14:02,554
What? Right now?

133
00:14:02,815 --> 00:14:05,398
<i>Yes. Now.</i>

134
00:14:06,194 --> 00:14:08,105
<i>Do it slowly.</i>

135
00:14:08,529 --> 00:14:09,735
<i>The elevator.</i>

136
00:14:14,619 --> 00:14:16,530
- Oh, shit!
- <i>Yes.</i>

137
00:14:21,125 --> 00:14:22,832
- What do they want?
- <i>I don't know.</i>

138
00:14:23,002 --> 00:14:25,994
<i>But if you don't want to find out,
get out of there.</i>

139
00:14:26,214 --> 00:14:27,454
- How?
- <i>I can guide you...</i>

140
00:14:27,632 --> 00:14:30,294
<i>...but you must do exactly
as I say.</i>

141
00:14:30,468 --> 00:14:33,085
- Okay.
- The <i>cubicle across from you is empty.</i>

142
00:14:36,265 --> 00:14:38,381
- But what if they--?
- <i>Go. Now.</i>

143
00:14:45,149 --> 00:14:47,516
<i>Stay here for just a moment.</i>

144
00:14:54,784 --> 00:14:57,492
<i>When I tell you,
go to the end of the row...</i>

145
00:14:57,662 --> 00:14:59,744
<i>...to the office
at the end of the hall.</i>

146
00:14:59,956 --> 00:15:02,323
<i>Stay as low as you can.</i>

147
00:15:04,502 --> 00:15:05,742
<i>Go. Now.</i>

148
00:15:20,226 --> 00:15:23,685
<i>Good. Now, outside
there is a scaffold.</i>

149
00:15:26,357 --> 00:15:28,769
- How do you know all this?
- We <i>don't have time.</i>

150
00:15:28,985 --> 00:15:31,852
<i>To your left there's a window.
Go to it.</i>

151
00:15:34,073 --> 00:15:35,563
<i>Open it.</i>

152
00:15:36,409 --> 00:15:38,275
<i>Use the scaffold to get
to the roof.</i>

153
00:15:38,494 --> 00:15:41,111
No way! No way!
This is crazy!

154
00:15:41,330 --> 00:15:43,697
<i>There are two ways
out of this building.</i>

155
00:15:43,916 --> 00:15:47,830
<i>One is that scaffold.
The other is in their custody.</i>

156
00:15:48,045 --> 00:15:51,163
<i>You take a chance either way.
I leave it to you.</i>

157
00:15:54,844 --> 00:15:56,505
This is insane!

158
00:15:57,722 --> 00:15:59,554
Why is this happening to me?

159
00:15:59,891 --> 00:16:01,507
What'd I do?

160
00:16:01,893 --> 00:16:04,681
I'm nobody.
I didn't do anything.

161
00:16:05,229 --> 00:16:06,719
I'm gonna die.

162
00:16:16,407 --> 00:16:17,647
Shit!

163
00:16:37,762 --> 00:16:38,968
Oh, shit!

164
00:16:43,935 --> 00:16:45,642
I can't do this.

165
00:16:58,407 --> 00:16:59,397
Shit.

166
00:17:48,666 --> 00:17:53,456
As you can see, we've had our eye
on you for some time now, Mr. Anderson.

167
00:17:54,797 --> 00:17:57,414
It seems that you've been living...

168
00:17:57,675 --> 00:17:59,791
...two lives.

169
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:03,757
In one life,
you're Thomas A. Anderson...

170
00:18:03,973 --> 00:18:07,341
...program writer for a respectable
software company.

171
00:18:08,352 --> 00:18:11,686
You have a social security number.
You pay your taxes.

172
00:18:12,064 --> 00:18:13,350
And you...

173
00:18:14,942 --> 00:18:18,560
...help your landlady
carry out her garbage.

174
00:18:21,073 --> 00:18:24,191
The other life is lived in computers...

175
00:18:24,452 --> 00:18:27,490
...where you go by
the hacker alias "Neo"...

176
00:18:27,705 --> 00:18:32,541
...and are guilty of virtually every
computer crime we have a law for.

177
00:18:33,836 --> 00:18:35,793
One of these lives...

178
00:18:36,005 --> 00:18:37,871
...has a future.

179
00:18:38,174 --> 00:18:40,131
And one of them does not.

180
00:18:43,888 --> 00:18:47,722
I'm going to be as forthcoming
as I can be, Mr. Anderson.

181
00:18:48,726 --> 00:18:50,057
You're here...

182
00:18:50,394 --> 00:18:52,601
...because we need your help.

183
00:18:56,275 --> 00:18:59,358
We know that you've been contacted
by a certain...

184
00:18:59,570 --> 00:19:01,311
...individual.

185
00:19:02,239 --> 00:19:06,233
A man who calls himself "Morpheus."

186
00:19:07,286 --> 00:19:11,280
Whatever you think you know
about this man is irrelevant.

187
00:19:11,499 --> 00:19:14,036
He is considered by many authorities...

188
00:19:14,251 --> 00:19:17,209
...to be the most dangerous man alive.

189
00:19:19,924 --> 00:19:21,164
My colleagues...

190
00:19:21,634 --> 00:19:24,592
...believe that I am wasting
my time with you.

191
00:19:24,845 --> 00:19:28,258
But I believe you wish
to do the right thing.

192
00:19:28,557 --> 00:19:32,050
We're willing to wipe the slate clean...

193
00:19:32,436 --> 00:19:34,518
...give you a fresh start.

194
00:19:35,106 --> 00:19:38,019
All that we're asking in return
is your cooperation...

195
00:19:38,234 --> 00:19:41,727
...in bringing
a known terrorist to justice.

196
00:19:43,114 --> 00:19:44,400
Yeah.

197
00:19:45,533 --> 00:19:47,740
Well, that sounds like a really good deal.

198
00:19:49,370 --> 00:19:51,111
But I think I got a better one.

199
00:19:51,330 --> 00:19:52,866
How about...

200
00:19:53,290 --> 00:19:55,281
... I give you the finger...

201
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:59,877
...and you give me my phone call.

202
00:20:02,133 --> 00:20:03,919
Mr. Anderson...

203
00:20:07,972 --> 00:20:09,178
...you disappoint me.

204
00:20:09,432 --> 00:20:12,049
You can't scare me
with this gestapo crap.

205
00:20:12,268 --> 00:20:13,679
I know my rights.

206
00:20:13,894 --> 00:20:15,384
I want my phone call.

207
00:20:15,980 --> 00:20:18,096
Tell me, Mr. Anderson...

208
00:20:19,024 --> 00:20:24,315
...what good is a phone call
if you're unable to speak?

209
00:20:58,063 --> 00:21:00,304
You're going to help us,
Mr. Anderson...

210
00:21:00,941 --> 00:21:03,023
...whether you want to or not.

211
00:22:01,377 --> 00:22:04,665
<i>This line is tapped,
so I must be brief.</i>

212
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:09,249
<i>They got to you first, but they've
underestimated how important you are.</i>

213
00:22:09,426 --> 00:22:11,258
<i>If they knew what I know...</i>

214
00:22:11,512 --> 00:22:13,503
<i>...you would probably be dead.</i>

215
00:22:14,557 --> 00:22:18,266
What are you talking about?
What is happening to me?

216
00:22:18,477 --> 00:22:23,313
<i>You are the One, Neo. You see,
you may have spent the last few years...</i>

217
00:22:23,524 --> 00:22:26,516
<i>...looking for me, but I've spent
my entire life...</i>

218
00:22:26,735 --> 00:22:28,271
<i>...looking for you.</i>

219
00:22:29,780 --> 00:22:31,942
<i>Now, do you still want to meet?</i>

220
00:22:32,950 --> 00:22:35,783
- Yes.
- <i>Then go to the Adams Street bridge.</i>

221
00:22:45,963 --> 00:22:47,203
Get in.

222
00:22:59,560 --> 00:23:02,222
- What the hell is this?
- It's necessary, Neo.

223
00:23:02,396 --> 00:23:04,387
- For our protection.
- From what?

224
00:23:04,648 --> 00:23:06,138
From you.

225
00:23:07,067 --> 00:23:08,603
- Take off your shirt.
- What?

226
00:23:09,153 --> 00:23:10,643
Stop the car.

227
00:23:14,450 --> 00:23:15,690
Listen to me, copper top.

228
00:23:15,910 --> 00:23:17,947
We don't have time for 20 Questions.

229
00:23:18,454 --> 00:23:20,741
Right now, there's only one rule:

230
00:23:21,081 --> 00:23:22,412
Our way...

231
00:23:22,583 --> 00:23:23,789
...or the highway.

232
00:23:30,466 --> 00:23:31,456
Fine.

233
00:23:33,344 --> 00:23:35,802
Please, Neo, you have to trust me.

234
00:23:36,347 --> 00:23:39,009
- Why?
- Because you have been down there, Neo.

235
00:23:39,767 --> 00:23:40,973
You know that road.

236
00:23:41,977 --> 00:23:43,593
You know exactly where it ends.

237
00:23:45,773 --> 00:23:48,014
And I know that's
not where you want to be.

238
00:24:02,247 --> 00:24:03,783
Apoc, lights.

239
00:24:06,377 --> 00:24:08,459
Lie back.
Lift up your shirt.

240
00:24:10,547 --> 00:24:13,380
- What is that thing?
- We think you're bugged.

241
00:24:20,391 --> 00:24:21,881
Try and relax.

242
00:24:28,065 --> 00:24:29,305
Come on.

243
00:24:30,442 --> 00:24:31,978
Come on.

244
00:24:33,237 --> 00:24:34,819
It's on the move.

245
00:24:35,906 --> 00:24:37,192
Come on, you shit.

246
00:24:38,993 --> 00:24:41,325
- You're gonna lose it.
- No, I'm not.

247
00:24:41,495 --> 00:24:43,156
Clear!

248
00:24:50,921 --> 00:24:53,253
Jesus Christ! That thing is real?!

249
00:25:26,957 --> 00:25:28,243
This is it.

250
00:25:31,628 --> 00:25:34,040
Let me give you one piece of advice.

251
00:25:35,090 --> 00:25:36,706
Be honest.

252
00:25:38,302 --> 00:25:40,464
He knows more than you can imagine.

253
00:25:49,271 --> 00:25:50,602
At last.

254
00:25:51,982 --> 00:25:53,222
Welcome, Neo.

255
00:25:54,401 --> 00:25:56,312
As you no doubt have guessed...

256
00:25:56,612 --> 00:25:57,818
... I am Morpheus.

257
00:25:58,864 --> 00:26:00,446
It's an honor to meet you.

258
00:26:00,824 --> 00:26:02,064
No...

259
00:26:02,534 --> 00:26:03,820
...the honor is mine.

260
00:26:04,745 --> 00:26:07,237
Please, come. Sit.

261
00:26:22,346 --> 00:26:23,962
I imagine...

262
00:26:24,389 --> 00:26:27,131
...that right now you're feeling
a bit like Alice.

263
00:26:28,852 --> 00:26:31,264
Tumbling down the rabbit hole?

264
00:26:32,189 --> 00:26:33,930
You could say that.

265
00:26:34,108 --> 00:26:36,691
I can see it in your eyes.

266
00:26:37,361 --> 00:26:40,649
You have the look of a man
who accepts what he sees...

267
00:26:40,864 --> 00:26:43,151
...because he's expecting to wake up.

268
00:26:44,535 --> 00:26:47,118
Ironically, this is not
far from the truth.

269
00:26:47,871 --> 00:26:50,283
Do you believe in fate, Neo?

270
00:26:50,749 --> 00:26:52,865
- No.
- Why not?

271
00:26:53,293 --> 00:26:56,706
Because I don't like the idea that
I'm not in control of my life.

272
00:26:57,047 --> 00:27:00,381
I know exactly what you mean.

273
00:27:04,721 --> 00:27:07,053
Let me tell you why you're here.

274
00:27:07,933 --> 00:27:11,847
You're here because you know something.
What you know, you can't explain.

275
00:27:12,271 --> 00:27:13,887
But you feel it.

276
00:27:14,481 --> 00:27:16,392
You felt it your entire life:

277
00:27:17,025 --> 00:27:21,189
There's something wrong with the world.
You don't know what, but it's there.

278
00:27:21,613 --> 00:27:23,900
Like a splinter in your mind...

279
00:27:24,116 --> 00:27:25,982
...driving you mad.

280
00:27:26,910 --> 00:27:29,698
It is this feeling
that has brought you to me.

281
00:27:32,166 --> 00:27:34,032
Do you know what
I'm talking about?

282
00:27:35,919 --> 00:27:37,205
The Matrix?

283
00:27:39,673 --> 00:27:41,380
Do you want to know...

284
00:27:41,717 --> 00:27:43,833
...what it is?

285
00:27:46,263 --> 00:27:48,129
The Matrix is everywhere.

286
00:27:48,348 --> 00:27:50,089
It is all around us.

287
00:27:50,309 --> 00:27:52,266
Even now, in this very room.

288
00:27:53,020 --> 00:27:55,432
You can see it when you
look out your window...

289
00:27:55,606 --> 00:27:57,938
...or when you turn on your television.

290
00:27:58,275 --> 00:28:00,892
You can feel it when you go to work...

291
00:28:02,362 --> 00:28:04,069
...when you go to church...

292
00:28:04,489 --> 00:28:06,571
...when you pay your taxes.

293
00:28:07,659 --> 00:28:10,617
It is the world that has been
pulled over your eyes...

294
00:28:10,829 --> 00:28:12,445
...to blind you from the truth.

295
00:28:14,625 --> 00:28:15,911
What truth?

296
00:28:20,130 --> 00:28:22,838
That you are a slave, Neo.

297
00:28:23,008 --> 00:28:25,545
Like everyone else,
you were born into bondage...

298
00:28:25,802 --> 00:28:30,421
...born into a prison that you cannot
smell or taste or touch.

299
00:28:30,766 --> 00:28:33,383
A prison for your mind.

300
00:28:40,400 --> 00:28:42,767
Unfortunately, no one can be...

301
00:28:43,028 --> 00:28:45,486
...told what the Matrix is.

302
00:28:48,951 --> 00:28:50,737
You have to see it for yourself.

303
00:29:00,337 --> 00:29:02,578
This is your last chance.

304
00:29:02,798 --> 00:29:05,165
After this, there is no turning back.

305
00:29:05,676 --> 00:29:07,087
You take the blue pill...

306
00:29:07,427 --> 00:29:10,510
...the story ends, you wake up
in your bed and believe...

307
00:29:10,722 --> 00:29:12,508
...whatever you want to believe.

308
00:29:12,766 --> 00:29:14,097
You take the red pill...

309
00:29:14,309 --> 00:29:16,266
...you stay in Wonderland...

310
00:29:16,853 --> 00:29:19,470
...and I show you how deep
the rabbit hole goes.

311
00:29:29,366 --> 00:29:30,606
Remember...

312
00:29:31,451 --> 00:29:34,443
...all I'm offering is the truth.
Nothing more.

313
00:29:48,844 --> 00:29:50,130
Follow me.

314
00:29:52,639 --> 00:29:54,380
Apoc, are we online?

315
00:29:54,599 --> 00:29:55,964
Almost.

316
00:29:59,354 --> 00:30:01,345
Time is always against us.

317
00:30:01,732 --> 00:30:03,222
Please, take a seat there.

318
00:30:21,418 --> 00:30:23,079
You did all this?

319
00:30:27,257 --> 00:30:29,919
The pill you took is
part of a trace program.

320
00:30:30,093 --> 00:30:34,633
It disrupts your input/output carrier signals
so we can pinpoint your location.

321
00:30:35,057 --> 00:30:36,263
What does that mean?

322
00:30:36,808 --> 00:30:38,970
It means buckle
your seat belt, Dorothy...

323
00:30:39,311 --> 00:30:41,894
...because Kansas is going bye-bye.

324
00:31:19,851 --> 00:31:21,262
Did you...?

325
00:31:32,239 --> 00:31:36,324
Have you ever had a dream, Neo,
that you were so sure was real?

326
00:31:37,828 --> 00:31:40,365
What if you were unable
to wake from that dream?

327
00:31:40,580 --> 00:31:43,698
How would you know the difference
between the dream world...

328
00:31:43,875 --> 00:31:45,161
...and the real world?

329
00:31:46,878 --> 00:31:49,165
- This can't be.
- Be what?

330
00:31:49,840 --> 00:31:51,376
Be real?

331
00:31:55,345 --> 00:31:56,835
It's going into replication.

332
00:31:57,013 --> 00:31:58,469
Still nothing.

333
00:31:58,682 --> 00:32:01,390
It's cold. It's cold!

334
00:32:05,230 --> 00:32:07,847
Tank, we're going to need a signal soon.

335
00:32:08,024 --> 00:32:09,355
I got a fibrillation.

336
00:32:09,568 --> 00:32:11,150
Apoc, location.

337
00:32:11,361 --> 00:32:12,817
Targeting almost there.

338
00:32:16,158 --> 00:32:17,523
He's going into arrest.

339
00:32:17,742 --> 00:32:19,653
- Lock. I got him!
- Now, Tank, now!

340
00:35:17,547 --> 00:35:18,833
Welcome...

341
00:35:19,007 --> 00:35:20,873
...to the real world.

342
00:35:22,344 --> 00:35:24,176
We've done it, Trinity.

343
00:35:24,387 --> 00:35:25,969
We found him.

344
00:35:26,181 --> 00:35:29,014
- I hope you're right.
- I don't have to hope.

345
00:35:29,559 --> 00:35:31,141
I know it.

346
00:35:36,191 --> 00:35:37,397
Am I dead?

347
00:35:37,817 --> 00:35:39,979
Far from it.

348
00:35:53,917 --> 00:35:55,453
He still needs a lot of work.

349
00:35:56,836 --> 00:35:58,042
What are you doing?

350
00:35:58,254 --> 00:36:01,042
Your muscles have atrophied.
We're rebuilding them.

351
00:36:01,216 --> 00:36:02,627
Why do my eyes hurt?

352
00:36:03,343 --> 00:36:05,254
You've never used them before.

353
00:36:09,140 --> 00:36:11,928
Rest, Neo. The answers are coming.

354
00:37:26,509 --> 00:37:28,625
Morpheus, what's happened to me?

355
00:37:28,845 --> 00:37:32,679
- What is this place?
- More important than "what" is "when."

356
00:37:33,516 --> 00:37:36,508
- "When"?
- You believe it's the year 1999...

357
00:37:36,728 --> 00:37:38,969
...when, in fact, it's closer to 2199.

358
00:37:40,106 --> 00:37:44,816
I can't tell you exactly what year it is
because we honestly don't know.

359
00:37:45,278 --> 00:37:48,145
There's nothing I can say
that will explain it for you.

360
00:37:48,364 --> 00:37:51,152
Come with me. See for yourself.

361
00:37:51,618 --> 00:37:53,359
This is my ship.

362
00:37:53,703 --> 00:37:56,570
The <i>Nebuchadnezzar.</i>
It's a hovercraft.

363
00:37:59,459 --> 00:38:01,200
This is the main deck.

364
00:38:07,217 --> 00:38:08,207
This is the core...

365
00:38:10,720 --> 00:38:14,509
...where we broadcast our pirate signal
and hack into the Matrix.

366
00:38:17,894 --> 00:38:20,977
Most of my crew you already know.

367
00:38:26,069 --> 00:38:27,434
This is Apoc...

368
00:38:28,238 --> 00:38:29,569
...Switch...

369
00:38:31,157 --> 00:38:32,363
- ...and Cypher.
- Hi.

370
00:38:32,575 --> 00:38:36,239
The ones you don't know,
Tank and his big brother, Dozer.

371
00:38:37,121 --> 00:38:39,579
The little one behind you is Mouse.

372
00:38:43,920 --> 00:38:47,208
You wanted to know
what the Matrix is, Neo?

373
00:38:48,216 --> 00:38:49,422
Trinity.

374
00:39:10,446 --> 00:39:12,062
Try to relax.

375
00:39:16,911 --> 00:39:18,777
This will feel a little weird.

376
00:39:30,758 --> 00:39:32,123
This...

377
00:39:32,302 --> 00:39:33,963
...is the Construct.

378
00:39:34,429 --> 00:39:36,511
It's our loading program.

379
00:39:36,723 --> 00:39:39,260
We can load anything, from clothing...

380
00:39:39,475 --> 00:39:40,806
...to equipment...

381
00:39:41,144 --> 00:39:42,475
...weapons...

382
00:39:43,104 --> 00:39:44,890
...training simulations...

383
00:39:45,315 --> 00:39:47,852
...anything we need.

384
00:39:50,653 --> 00:39:53,111
Right now we're inside
a computer program?

385
00:39:53,323 --> 00:39:55,314
Is it really so hard to believe?

386
00:39:55,783 --> 00:39:59,151
Your clothes are different.
The plugs in your body are gone.

387
00:39:59,579 --> 00:40:01,661
Your hair has changed.

388
00:40:02,123 --> 00:40:05,411
Your appearance now is what we call
"residual self-image."

389
00:40:06,169 --> 00:40:08,752
It is the mental projection
of your digital self.

390
00:40:14,677 --> 00:40:17,510
- This isn't real?
- What is "real"?

391
00:40:17,972 --> 00:40:20,179
How do you define "real"?

392
00:40:20,391 --> 00:40:25,101
If you're talking about what you can feel,
what you can smell, taste and see...

393
00:40:25,313 --> 00:40:29,181
...then "real" is simply electrical
signals interpreted by your brain.

394
00:40:33,363 --> 00:40:35,821
This is the world that you know.

395
00:40:37,200 --> 00:40:40,192
The world as it was at the end
of the 20th century.

396
00:40:42,622 --> 00:40:47,037
It exists now only as part of
a neural-interactive simulation...

397
00:40:47,210 --> 00:40:48,996
...that we call the Matrix.

398
00:40:53,007 --> 00:40:55,795
You've been living
in a dream world, Neo.

399
00:40:56,761 --> 00:40:59,970
This is the world as it exists today.

400
00:41:13,069 --> 00:41:16,027
Welcome to the desert...

401
00:41:16,823 --> 00:41:18,439
...of the real.

402
00:41:21,828 --> 00:41:24,240
We have only bits and pieces
of information.

403
00:41:24,414 --> 00:41:28,248
But what we know for certain is that
in the early 21st century...

404
00:41:28,459 --> 00:41:31,747
...all of mankind was united
in celebration.

405
00:41:31,963 --> 00:41:36,753
We marveled at our own magnificence
as we gave birth to AI.

406
00:41:37,427 --> 00:41:38,667
Al.

407
00:41:39,470 --> 00:41:41,086
You mean artificial intelligence.

408
00:41:41,264 --> 00:41:45,758
A singular consciousness that spawned
an entire race of machines.

409
00:41:46,602 --> 00:41:50,061
We don't know who struck first,
us or them.

410
00:41:50,440 --> 00:41:53,728
But we know that it was us
that scorched the sky.

411
00:41:55,403 --> 00:41:57,519
They were dependent on solar power...

412
00:41:57,739 --> 00:42:01,107
...and it was believed that
they would be unable to survive...

413
00:42:01,451 --> 00:42:04,944
...without an energy source
as abundant as the sun.

414
00:42:05,163 --> 00:42:10,124
Throughout human history, we have been
dependent on machines to survive.

415
00:42:11,586 --> 00:42:15,750
Fate, it seems, is not
without a sense of irony.

416
00:42:18,968 --> 00:42:23,383
The human body generates more
bio electricity than a 120-volt battery.

417
00:42:23,598 --> 00:42:27,717
And over 25,000 BTUs of body heat.

418
00:42:29,645 --> 00:42:31,807
Combined with a form of fusion...

419
00:42:32,190 --> 00:42:36,980
...the machines had found all the energy
they would ever need.

420
00:42:41,115 --> 00:42:44,824
There are fields, Neo, endless fields...

421
00:42:45,119 --> 00:42:48,328
...where human beings
are no longer born.

422
00:42:49,040 --> 00:42:50,872
We are grown.

423
00:42:56,881 --> 00:42:59,543
For the longest time,
I wouldn't believe it.

424
00:42:59,759 --> 00:43:02,467
And then I saw the fields
with my own eyes...

425
00:43:03,679 --> 00:43:05,511
...watched them liquefy the dead...

426
00:43:05,681 --> 00:43:09,015
...so they could be fed intravenously
to the living.

427
00:43:09,519 --> 00:43:13,763
And standing there,
facing the pure, horrifying precision...

428
00:43:13,981 --> 00:43:16,939
...I came to realize
the obviousness of the truth.

429
00:43:19,570 --> 00:43:21,356
What is the Matrix?

430
00:43:22,406 --> 00:43:23,646
Control.

431
00:43:24,992 --> 00:43:28,360
The Matrix is a computer-generated
dream world...

432
00:43:29,122 --> 00:43:32,205
...built to keep us under control...

433
00:43:33,417 --> 00:43:36,535
...in order to change a human being...

434
00:43:37,213 --> 00:43:38,419
...into this.

435
00:43:39,715 --> 00:43:40,921
No.

436
00:43:42,552 --> 00:43:44,088
I don't believe it.

437
00:43:44,470 --> 00:43:45,676
It's not possible.

438
00:43:46,264 --> 00:43:49,052
I didn't say it would be easy, Neo.

439
00:43:49,684 --> 00:43:52,472
- I just said it would be the truth.
- Stop!

440
00:43:52,895 --> 00:43:54,101
Let me out!

441
00:43:54,897 --> 00:43:56,763
Let me out! I want out!

442
00:43:58,734 --> 00:44:01,396
- Easy, Neo. Easy.
- Get this thing out of me.

443
00:44:01,612 --> 00:44:03,319
Get this thing out of me!

444
00:44:05,116 --> 00:44:08,484
Don't touch me! Get away from me!
Stay away from me!

445
00:44:08,911 --> 00:44:10,401
I don't believe it.

446
00:44:11,080 --> 00:44:12,366
I don't believe it.

447
00:44:12,665 --> 00:44:15,498
- I don't believe it.
- He's gonna pop.

448
00:44:15,668 --> 00:44:17,830
Breathe, Neo. Just breathe.

449
00:44:36,272 --> 00:44:37,979
I can't go back, can I?

450
00:44:38,858 --> 00:44:40,064
No.

451
00:44:41,110 --> 00:44:42,316
But if you could...

452
00:44:43,112 --> 00:44:44,602
...would you really want to?

453
00:44:47,116 --> 00:44:50,450
I feel I owe you an apology.
We have a rule:

454
00:44:50,953 --> 00:44:54,366
We never free a mind
once it's reached a certain age.

455
00:44:54,582 --> 00:44:56,072
It's dangerous.

456
00:44:56,250 --> 00:44:57,957
The mind has trouble letting go.

457
00:44:58,127 --> 00:45:00,459
I've seen it before, and I'm sorry.

458
00:45:01,464 --> 00:45:03,546
I did what I did because...

459
00:45:04,300 --> 00:45:05,756
... I had to.

460
00:45:14,143 --> 00:45:18,262
When the Matrix was first built,
there was a man born inside...

461
00:45:18,689 --> 00:45:22,523
...who had the ability
to change whatever he wanted...

462
00:45:22,944 --> 00:45:25,811
...to remake the Matrix as he saw fit.

463
00:45:27,573 --> 00:45:31,032
It was he who freed the first of us...

464
00:45:31,953 --> 00:45:33,535
...taught us the truth.

465
00:45:34,997 --> 00:45:38,080
As long as the Matrix exists...

466
00:45:38,376 --> 00:45:40,458
...the human race will never be free.

467
00:45:44,674 --> 00:45:46,256
After he died...

468
00:45:47,009 --> 00:45:49,717
...the Oracle prophesied his return...

469
00:45:50,096 --> 00:45:53,555
...and that his coming would hail
the destruction of the Matrix...

470
00:45:53,724 --> 00:45:55,465
...end the war...

471
00:45:55,685 --> 00:45:58,017
...bring freedom to our people.

472
00:45:58,312 --> 00:46:03,102
That is why there are those of us who have
spent our entire lives searching the Matrix...

473
00:46:03,276 --> 00:46:04,812
...looking for him.

474
00:46:07,280 --> 00:46:09,362
I did what I did because...

475
00:46:11,033 --> 00:46:13,115
... I believe that search is over.

476
00:46:18,207 --> 00:46:19,618
Get some rest.

477
00:46:20,251 --> 00:46:22,037
You're going to need it.

478
00:46:25,047 --> 00:46:26,503
For what?

479
00:46:29,093 --> 00:46:30,800
Your training.

480
00:46:48,321 --> 00:46:50,062
Morning. Did you sleep?

481
00:46:50,906 --> 00:46:52,317
You will tonight.

482
00:46:52,491 --> 00:46:54,073
I guarantee it.

483
00:46:55,578 --> 00:46:57,535
I'm Tank. I'll be your operator.

484
00:46:57,913 --> 00:47:01,031
- You don't-- You don't have any--
- Holes? Nope.

485
00:47:01,250 --> 00:47:04,083
Me and my brother Dozer,
we're both 100 percent pure...

486
00:47:04,253 --> 00:47:06,085
...old-fashioned, homegrown human.

487
00:47:06,255 --> 00:47:07,461
Born free right here...

488
00:47:08,049 --> 00:47:09,335
...in the real world.

489
00:47:09,592 --> 00:47:11,208
Genuine child of Zion.

490
00:47:12,094 --> 00:47:14,552
- Of Zion?
- If the war was over tomorrow...

491
00:47:14,764 --> 00:47:17,973
- ...Zion's where the party would be.
- It's a city?

492
00:47:18,142 --> 00:47:21,430
The last human city.
The only place we have left.

493
00:47:23,022 --> 00:47:24,262
Where is it?

494
00:47:25,983 --> 00:47:29,442
Deep underground, near the Earth's core,
where it's still warm.

495
00:47:31,072 --> 00:47:33,689
You live long enough,
you might even see it.

496
00:47:35,159 --> 00:47:40,199
Goddamn! I gotta tell you, I'm excited
to see what you're capable of...

497
00:47:40,373 --> 00:47:42,080
...if Morpheus is right and all.

498
00:47:42,500 --> 00:47:45,333
We're not supposed to
talk about this, but...

499
00:47:45,544 --> 00:47:46,955
...if you are...

500
00:47:48,005 --> 00:47:49,996
...it's a very exciting time.

501
00:47:51,133 --> 00:47:53,795
We got a lot to do.
We gotta get to it.

502
00:47:56,097 --> 00:47:57,553
Now...

503
00:47:57,723 --> 00:48:01,387
We're supposed to start
with these operation programs first.

504
00:48:01,644 --> 00:48:05,103
That's major boring shit.
Let's do something a little more fun.

505
00:48:05,439 --> 00:48:06,895
How about...

506
00:48:08,484 --> 00:48:10,225
...combat training?

507
00:48:16,283 --> 00:48:17,739
"Jujitsu"?

508
00:48:18,661 --> 00:48:20,277
I'm going to learn jujitsu?

509
00:48:31,632 --> 00:48:32,838
Holy shit!

510
00:48:33,134 --> 00:48:35,421
"Hey, Mikey, I think he likes it."

511
00:48:35,803 --> 00:48:37,089
How about some more?

512
00:48:37,304 --> 00:48:38,635
Hell, yes.

513
00:48:40,850 --> 00:48:42,090
Hell, yeah.

514
00:48:54,071 --> 00:48:57,405
- How is he?
- Ten hours straight. He's a machine.

515
00:49:08,669 --> 00:49:10,034
I know kung fu.

516
00:49:11,672 --> 00:49:12,662
Show me.

517
00:49:14,508 --> 00:49:16,249
This is a sparring program...

518
00:49:16,469 --> 00:49:19,211
...similar to the programmed reality
of the Matrix.

519
00:49:19,388 --> 00:49:21,880
It has the same basic rules.
Rules like gravity.

520
00:49:22,099 --> 00:49:25,558
These rules are no different
than the rules of a computer system.

521
00:49:26,103 --> 00:49:27,639
Some of them can be bent.

522
00:49:27,855 --> 00:49:30,222
Others can be broken.

523
00:49:30,941 --> 00:49:32,648
Understand?

524
00:49:33,277 --> 00:49:35,735
Then hit me, if you can.

525
00:50:14,944 --> 00:50:16,309
Good!

526
00:50:16,487 --> 00:50:19,229
Adaptation, improvisation.

527
00:50:19,490 --> 00:50:20,855
But your weakness...

528
00:50:21,075 --> 00:50:22,440
...is not your technique.

529
00:50:29,375 --> 00:50:31,241
Morpheus is fighting Neo.

530
00:51:43,741 --> 00:51:44,981
How did I beat you?

531
00:51:51,373 --> 00:51:52,613
You're too fast.

532
00:51:53,125 --> 00:51:54,536
Do you believe that...

533
00:51:54,877 --> 00:51:57,369
...my being stronger or faster...

534
00:51:57,630 --> 00:52:01,339
...has anything to do
with my muscles in this place?

535
00:52:05,304 --> 00:52:08,171
You think that's air you're breathing now?

536
00:52:20,653 --> 00:52:21,859
Again!

537
00:52:33,332 --> 00:52:35,744
Jesus Christ, he's fast!

538
00:52:35,918 --> 00:52:38,250
His neuro-kinetics,
they're way above normal.

539
00:52:43,717 --> 00:52:45,128
What are you waiting for?

540
00:52:45,386 --> 00:52:47,343
You're faster than this.

541
00:52:49,598 --> 00:52:51,760
Don't think you are.

542
00:52:52,059 --> 00:52:53,720
Know you are.

543
00:53:04,113 --> 00:53:06,855
Come on! Stop trying to hit me,
and hit me!

544
00:53:16,792 --> 00:53:18,408
I don't believe it.

545
00:53:20,129 --> 00:53:22,211
I know what you're trying to do.

546
00:53:23,841 --> 00:53:26,048
I'm trying to free your mind, Neo.

547
00:53:26,385 --> 00:53:30,879
But I can only show you the door.
You're the one that has to walk through it.

548
00:53:33,225 --> 00:53:35,432
Tank, load the jump program.

549
00:53:46,989 --> 00:53:49,651
You have to let it all go, Neo.
Fear...

550
00:53:50,242 --> 00:53:52,449
...doubt and disbelief.

551
00:53:53,620 --> 00:53:56,282
Free your mind.

552
00:54:12,431 --> 00:54:14,172
Okey-dokey.

553
00:54:16,185 --> 00:54:17,425
Free my mind.

554
00:54:18,145 --> 00:54:21,183
- What if he makes it?
- No one's ever made their first jump.

555
00:54:21,356 --> 00:54:23,063
I know, I know.

556
00:54:23,317 --> 00:54:25,775
- But what if he does?
- He won't.

557
00:54:26,445 --> 00:54:27,435
Come on.

558
00:54:27,696 --> 00:54:29,107
All right.

559
00:54:29,281 --> 00:54:31,363
No problem. Free my mind.

560
00:54:32,201 --> 00:54:34,943
Free my mind. No problem. Right.

561
00:54:54,348 --> 00:54:56,009
What does that mean?

562
00:54:56,391 --> 00:54:58,223
It doesn't mean anything.

563
00:54:58,852 --> 00:55:01,389
Everybody falls the first time.

564
00:55:01,855 --> 00:55:03,141
Right, Trin?

565
00:55:23,794 --> 00:55:26,502
- I thought it wasn't real.
- Your mind makes it real.

566
00:55:29,675 --> 00:55:31,916
If you're killed in the Matrix...

567
00:55:32,469 --> 00:55:35,461
- ...you die here?
- The body cannot live without the mind.

568
00:56:06,795 --> 00:56:10,129
I don't remember you ever
bringing me dinner.

569
00:56:13,218 --> 00:56:16,051
There is something about him,
isn't there?

570
00:56:16,471 --> 00:56:18,337
Don't tell me
you're a believer now.

571
00:56:19,308 --> 00:56:22,300
I just keep wondering,
if Morpheus is so sure...

572
00:56:22,477 --> 00:56:25,014
...why doesn't he take him
to see the Oracle?

573
00:56:25,188 --> 00:56:28,271
Morpheus will take him
when he's ready.

574
00:56:38,076 --> 00:56:39,612
The Matrix is a system, Neo.

575
00:56:41,330 --> 00:56:42,661
That system is our enemy.

576
00:56:43,332 --> 00:56:45,664
But when you're inside,
what do you see?

577
00:56:45,834 --> 00:56:49,668
Businessmen, teachers,
lawyers, carpenters.

578
00:56:50,088 --> 00:56:52,750
The very minds of the people
we are trying to save.

579
00:56:52,966 --> 00:56:55,958
But until we do, these people are
a part of that system...

580
00:56:56,178 --> 00:56:58,215
...and that makes them our enemy.

581
00:56:58,388 --> 00:57:03,007
You have to understand, most of these
people are not ready to be unplugged.

582
00:57:03,185 --> 00:57:04,892
And many of them are so inert...

583
00:57:05,062 --> 00:57:07,554
...so hopelessly dependent
on the system...

584
00:57:07,773 --> 00:57:10,515
...that they will fight to protect it.

585
00:57:12,027 --> 00:57:15,770
Were you listening to me, Neo,
or looking at the woman in the red dress?

586
00:57:16,156 --> 00:57:17,738
- I was--
- Look again.

587
00:57:18,909 --> 00:57:20,491
Freeze it.

588
00:57:26,625 --> 00:57:28,957
- This isn't the Matrix?
- No.

589
00:57:30,087 --> 00:57:33,876
It's another training program
designed to teach you one thing:

590
00:57:34,549 --> 00:57:37,007
If you are not one of us,
you are one of them.

591
00:57:37,552 --> 00:57:40,294
- What are they?
- Sentient programs.

592
00:57:41,056 --> 00:57:45,345
They can move in and out of any software
still hardwired to their system.

593
00:57:45,727 --> 00:57:49,095
That means that anyone
we haven't unplugged...

594
00:57:49,272 --> 00:57:50,728
...is potentially an agent.

595
00:57:51,733 --> 00:57:53,565
Inside the Matrix...

596
00:57:54,194 --> 00:57:55,855
...they are everyone...

597
00:57:56,154 --> 00:57:57,895
...and they are no one.

598
00:57:58,115 --> 00:58:01,358
We have survived by hiding from them
and running from them...

599
00:58:01,535 --> 00:58:03,196
...but they are the gatekeepers.

600
00:58:03,412 --> 00:58:06,404
They're guarding all the doors
and holding all the keys.

601
00:58:06,623 --> 00:58:09,411
Sooner or later, someone will
have to fight them.

602
00:58:09,668 --> 00:58:10,874
Someone?

603
00:58:11,086 --> 00:58:12,542
I won't lie to you, Neo.

604
00:58:12,963 --> 00:58:15,079
Every single man or woman...

605
00:58:15,257 --> 00:58:17,999
...everyone who has fought an agent,
has died.

606
00:58:18,176 --> 00:58:20,543
But where they have failed,
you will succeed.

607
00:58:20,846 --> 00:58:21,836
Why?

608
00:58:22,014 --> 00:58:24,346
I've seen an agent punch
through a concrete wall.

609
00:58:24,558 --> 00:58:28,176
Men have emptied entire clips at them
and hit nothing but air.

610
00:58:28,395 --> 00:58:33,060
Yet their strength and their speed are still
based in a world that is built on rules.

611
00:58:33,233 --> 00:58:34,473
Because of that...

612
00:58:34,651 --> 00:58:38,019
...they will never be as strong
or as fast as you can be.

613
00:58:42,325 --> 00:58:44,191
What are you trying to tell me?

614
00:58:44,911 --> 00:58:46,367
That I can dodge bullets?

615
00:58:48,373 --> 00:58:49,784
No, Neo.

616
00:58:50,250 --> 00:58:53,163
I'm trying to tell you
that when you're ready...

617
00:58:54,004 --> 00:58:55,369
...you won't have to.

618
00:58:59,718 --> 00:59:00,708
<i>We got trouble.</i>

619
00:59:19,654 --> 00:59:22,066
- Did Zion send the warning?
- No, another ship.

620
00:59:25,327 --> 00:59:26,692
Shit.

621
00:59:26,912 --> 00:59:28,619
Squiddy's sweeping in quick.

622
00:59:29,039 --> 00:59:30,700
- Squiddy?
- A sentinel.

623
00:59:30,874 --> 00:59:33,286
A killing machine
designed for one thing.

624
00:59:33,460 --> 00:59:34,666
Search and destroy.

625
00:59:35,962 --> 00:59:37,748
Set her down right over there.

626
00:59:58,735 --> 00:59:59,975
How are we doing, Tank?

627
01:00:08,662 --> 01:00:09,868
Power off-line.

628
01:00:10,288 --> 01:00:12,279
EMP armed...

629
01:00:12,874 --> 01:00:14,330
- <i>...and ready.</i>
- EMP?

630
01:00:14,709 --> 01:00:16,575
Electromagnetic pulse.

631
01:00:16,795 --> 01:00:19,753
Disables any electrical system
in the blast radius.

632
01:00:19,923 --> 01:00:22,881
It's the only weapon we have
against the machines.

633
01:00:28,056 --> 01:00:31,014
- Where are we?
- Their old service and waste systems.

634
01:00:32,561 --> 01:00:34,393
- Sewers.
- There used to be cities...

635
01:00:34,563 --> 01:00:38,773
...that spanned hundreds of miles. Now
these sewers are all that's left of them.

636
01:00:38,942 --> 01:00:40,307
Quiet.

637
01:01:24,237 --> 01:01:26,399
You scared the bejesus out of me.

638
01:01:27,449 --> 01:01:29,406
- Sorry.
- It's okay.

639
01:01:32,495 --> 01:01:34,953
- Is that...?
- The Matrix?

640
01:01:35,415 --> 01:01:36,826
Yeah.

641
01:01:38,168 --> 01:01:41,411
- Do you always look at it encoded?
- Well, you have to.

642
01:01:41,588 --> 01:01:44,751
The image translators work
for the construct program.

643
01:01:44,966 --> 01:01:48,379
But there's way too much information
to decode the Matrix.

644
01:01:48,595 --> 01:01:51,553
You get used to it.
I don't even see the code.

645
01:01:51,765 --> 01:01:55,224
All I see is blonde, brunette, redhead.

646
01:01:55,477 --> 01:01:57,718
Hey, do you...

647
01:01:58,063 --> 01:02:00,475
- ...want a drink?
- Sure.

648
01:02:03,985 --> 01:02:05,475
You know...

649
01:02:06,154 --> 01:02:07,770
... I know what you're thinking.

650
01:02:07,989 --> 01:02:10,230
Because right now I'm thinking
the same thing.

651
01:02:10,617 --> 01:02:13,951
Actually, I've been thinking it
ever since I got here.

652
01:02:15,830 --> 01:02:18,822
Why, oh, why didn't I take
the blue pill?

653
01:02:31,221 --> 01:02:33,132
Good shit, huh?

654
01:02:33,473 --> 01:02:34,679
Dozer makes it.

655
01:02:35,100 --> 01:02:39,594
It's good for two things:
Degreasing engines and killing brain cells.

656
01:02:40,689 --> 01:02:42,851
So can I ask you something?

657
01:02:45,860 --> 01:02:47,476
Did he tell you why he did it?

658
01:02:50,115 --> 01:02:51,947
Why you're here?

659
01:02:55,662 --> 01:02:57,369
Jesus!

660
01:02:58,581 --> 01:03:00,447
What a mind job.

661
01:03:01,918 --> 01:03:04,706
So you're here to save the world.

662
01:03:06,214 --> 01:03:08,296
What do you say
to something like that?

663
01:03:13,471 --> 01:03:14,836
A little piece of advice.

664
01:03:16,683 --> 01:03:18,048
You see an agent...

665
01:03:18,393 --> 01:03:20,725
...you do what we do.

666
01:03:21,021 --> 01:03:22,557
Run.

667
01:03:22,897 --> 01:03:24,638
You run your ass off.

668
01:03:31,906 --> 01:03:33,567
Thanks for the drink.

669
01:03:38,288 --> 01:03:39,528
Sweet dreams.

670
01:03:43,501 --> 01:03:46,914
Do we have a deal, Mr. Reagan?

671
01:03:47,464 --> 01:03:48,704
You know...

672
01:03:50,175 --> 01:03:52,587
... I know this steak doesn't exist.

673
01:03:53,595 --> 01:03:56,383
I know that when I put it
in my mouth...

674
01:03:56,598 --> 01:03:59,636
...the Matrix is telling my brain
that it is...

675
01:03:59,893 --> 01:04:01,179
...juicy...

676
01:04:01,353 --> 01:04:03,060
...and delicious.

677
01:04:06,024 --> 01:04:07,230
After nine years...

678
01:04:08,318 --> 01:04:09,854
...you know what I realize?

679
01:04:17,702 --> 01:04:18,908
Ignorance is bliss.

680
01:04:23,958 --> 01:04:25,790
Then we have a deal.

681
01:04:28,296 --> 01:04:30,287
I don't want to remember nothing.

682
01:04:30,465 --> 01:04:32,957
Nothing. You understand?

683
01:04:37,013 --> 01:04:38,845
And I want to be rich.

684
01:04:40,141 --> 01:04:42,883
You know, someone important.

685
01:04:44,312 --> 01:04:45,552
Like an actor.

686
01:04:46,731 --> 01:04:49,814
Whatever you want, Mr. Reagan.

687
01:04:52,070 --> 01:04:53,560
Okay.

688
01:04:53,947 --> 01:04:56,359
You get my body
back in a power plant...

689
01:04:56,741 --> 01:05:00,234
...reinsert me into the Matrix,
I'll get you what you want.

690
01:05:00,495 --> 01:05:02,486
Access codes to the Zion mainframe.

691
01:05:02,747 --> 01:05:04,909
No. I told you, I don't know them.

692
01:05:07,877 --> 01:05:09,834
I can get you the man who does.

693
01:05:10,588 --> 01:05:12,420
Morpheus.

694
01:05:22,559 --> 01:05:26,018
Here you go, buddy.
Breakfast of champions.

695
01:05:27,188 --> 01:05:30,146
Close your eyes, it feels
like you're eating runny eggs.

696
01:05:30,358 --> 01:05:31,940
Yeah, or a bowl of snot.

697
01:05:32,360 --> 01:05:34,192
Do you know what it reminds me of?

698
01:05:35,947 --> 01:05:38,359
Tastee Wheat. Did you
ever eat Tastee Wheat?

699
01:05:38,783 --> 01:05:40,694
No, but technically,
neither did you.

700
01:05:40,869 --> 01:05:42,735
That's exactly my point. Exactly.

701
01:05:42,912 --> 01:05:44,653
Because you have to wonder now...

702
01:05:44,831 --> 01:05:48,199
...how do the machines really know
what Tastee Wheat tasted like?

703
01:05:48,376 --> 01:05:49,787
Maybe they got it wrong.

704
01:05:49,961 --> 01:05:53,454
Maybe what I think Tastee Wheat
tasted like actually tasted like...

705
01:05:53,631 --> 01:05:55,542
...oatmeal or tuna fish.

706
01:05:55,884 --> 01:05:58,717
That makes you wonder.
Take chicken, for example.

707
01:05:58,887 --> 01:06:01,254
Maybe they didn't know
what to make it taste like...

708
01:06:01,431 --> 01:06:03,342
...which is why it tastes
like everything.

709
01:06:03,558 --> 01:06:05,344
- And maybe they--
- Shut up, Mouse.

710
01:06:06,811 --> 01:06:08,427
It's a single-celled protein...

711
01:06:08,605 --> 01:06:11,688
...combined with synthetic aminos,
vitamins and minerals.

712
01:06:11,858 --> 01:06:13,223
Everything the body needs.

713
01:06:13,401 --> 01:06:16,268
It doesn't have everything
the body needs.

714
01:06:19,073 --> 01:06:22,862
So I understand that you've run
through the agent training program.

715
01:06:23,244 --> 01:06:25,235
You know, I wrote that program.

716
01:06:25,497 --> 01:06:26,908
Here it comes.

717
01:06:27,081 --> 01:06:29,072
- What did you think of her?
- Of who?

718
01:06:29,417 --> 01:06:32,455
The woman in the red dress.
I designed her.

719
01:06:32,754 --> 01:06:35,587
She doesn't talk very much...

720
01:06:35,798 --> 01:06:39,792
...but if you'd like to meet her,
I can arrange a more personal milieu.

721
01:06:39,969 --> 01:06:43,928
- The digital pimp hard at work.
- Pay no attention to these hypocrites, Neo.

722
01:06:45,225 --> 01:06:47,091
To deny our own impulses...

723
01:06:47,268 --> 01:06:50,386
...is to deny the very thing
that makes us human.

724
01:06:52,190 --> 01:06:55,399
Dozer, when you're done,
bring the ship up to broadcast depth.

725
01:06:56,027 --> 01:06:57,438
We're going in.

726
01:06:58,112 --> 01:06:59,523
I'm taking Neo to see her.

727
01:07:03,952 --> 01:07:05,568
See who?

728
01:07:05,745 --> 01:07:06,951
The Oracle.

729
01:07:12,460 --> 01:07:13,950
Everyone please observe...

730
01:07:14,128 --> 01:07:17,086
...the "fasten seat belt"
and "no smoking" signs are on.

731
01:07:17,590 --> 01:07:20,958
Sit back and enjoy your flight.

732
01:07:44,701 --> 01:07:45,691
We're in.

733
01:08:01,801 --> 01:08:03,166
We'll be back in an hour.

734
01:08:17,984 --> 01:08:19,349
Unbelievable...

735
01:08:20,194 --> 01:08:21,525
...isn't it?

736
01:08:25,116 --> 01:08:26,982
- God!
- What?

737
01:08:27,619 --> 01:08:29,030
I used to eat there.

738
01:08:31,247 --> 01:08:32,829
Really good noodles.

739
01:08:37,712 --> 01:08:40,124
I have these memories from my life.

740
01:08:42,634 --> 01:08:44,341
None of them happened.

741
01:08:45,053 --> 01:08:46,293
What does that mean?

742
01:08:46,471 --> 01:08:48,712
That the Matrix cannot tell you
who you are.

743
01:08:49,682 --> 01:08:52,515
- But an oracle can?
- That's different.

744
01:08:57,607 --> 01:08:59,189
Did you go to her?

745
01:08:59,984 --> 01:09:01,190
Yes.

746
01:09:01,736 --> 01:09:03,067
What did she tell you?

747
01:09:06,324 --> 01:09:07,814
She told me...

748
01:09:08,868 --> 01:09:10,074
What?

749
01:09:13,831 --> 01:09:15,162
We're here.

750
01:09:15,458 --> 01:09:17,825
Neo, come with me.

751
01:09:37,814 --> 01:09:40,431
So is this the same oracle
that made...

752
01:09:40,817 --> 01:09:42,899
- ...the prophecy?
- Yes.

753
01:09:43,111 --> 01:09:46,229
She's very old. She's been
with us since the beginning.

754
01:09:46,698 --> 01:09:48,735
- The beginning?
- Of the Resistance.

755
01:09:50,952 --> 01:09:53,284
And she knows what? Everything?

756
01:09:55,331 --> 01:09:57,288
She would say she knows enough.

757
01:09:58,459 --> 01:10:00,200
Then she's never wrong.

758
01:10:02,422 --> 01:10:05,585
Try not to think of it
in terms of right and wrong.

759
01:10:05,967 --> 01:10:07,503
She is a guide, Neo.

760
01:10:07,885 --> 01:10:09,751
She can help you to find the path.

761
01:10:10,596 --> 01:10:13,258
- She helped you?
- Yes.

762
01:10:13,975 --> 01:10:15,340
What did she tell you?

763
01:10:17,812 --> 01:10:19,598
That I would find the One.

764
01:10:33,202 --> 01:10:35,284
I told you I can only
show you the door.

765
01:10:35,997 --> 01:10:38,034
You have to walk through it.

766
01:10:41,836 --> 01:10:44,874
Hello, Neo.
You're right on time.

767
01:10:52,764 --> 01:10:56,553
Make yourself at home, Morpheus.
Neo, come with me.

768
01:11:02,231 --> 01:11:03,847
These are the other Potentials.

769
01:11:04,066 --> 01:11:05,648
You can wait here.

770
01:11:46,484 --> 01:11:49,021
Do not try and bend the spoon.

771
01:11:49,403 --> 01:11:51,519
That's impossible.

772
01:11:52,365 --> 01:11:56,359
Instead, only try
to realize the truth.

773
01:11:56,911 --> 01:11:58,276
What truth?

774
01:11:58,496 --> 01:12:00,203
There is no spoon.

775
01:12:02,792 --> 01:12:04,157
There is no spoon?

776
01:12:04,377 --> 01:12:08,837
Then you'll see that it is not the spoon
that bends. It is only yourself.

777
01:12:24,897 --> 01:12:26,353
The Oracle will you see now.

778
01:12:36,993 --> 01:12:38,609
I know you're Neo.

779
01:12:39,120 --> 01:12:40,360
Be right with you.

780
01:12:41,497 --> 01:12:44,455
- You're the Oracle?
- Bingo.

781
01:12:46,502 --> 01:12:49,369
Not quite what you
were expecting, right?

782
01:12:50,464 --> 01:12:52,580
Almost done.

783
01:12:55,136 --> 01:12:56,672
Smell good, don't they?

784
01:12:58,514 --> 01:13:01,381
- Yeah.
- I'd ask you to sit down...

785
01:13:01,559 --> 01:13:03,971
...but you're not going to anyway.

786
01:13:04,478 --> 01:13:07,311
- And don't worry about the vase.
- What vase?

787
01:13:10,484 --> 01:13:11,690
That vase.

788
01:13:12,486 --> 01:13:13,692
I'm sorry.

789
01:13:13,863 --> 01:13:15,729
I said, don't worry about it.

790
01:13:16,949 --> 01:13:18,906
I'll get one of my kids to fix it.

791
01:13:19,493 --> 01:13:20,699
How did you know?

792
01:13:22,705 --> 01:13:26,573
What's really going to bake
your noodle later on is...

793
01:13:26,751 --> 01:13:29,869
...would you still have broken it
if I hadn't said anything?

794
01:13:34,675 --> 01:13:36,541
You're cuter than I thought.

795
01:13:39,597 --> 01:13:41,838
I can see why she likes you.

796
01:13:42,767 --> 01:13:45,885
- Who?
- Not too bright, though.

797
01:13:49,190 --> 01:13:51,477
You know why Morpheus
brought you to see me.

798
01:13:54,403 --> 01:13:55,643
So...

799
01:13:56,530 --> 01:13:57,895
...what do you think?

800
01:13:59,784 --> 01:14:01,491
Do you think you are the One?

801
01:14:03,537 --> 01:14:05,323
Honestly, I don't know.

802
01:14:07,917 --> 01:14:09,373
You know what that means?

803
01:14:10,211 --> 01:14:11,542
It's Latin.

804
01:14:11,712 --> 01:14:13,953
Means, "Know thyself."

805
01:14:15,383 --> 01:14:17,374
I'll let you in on a little secret.

806
01:14:19,595 --> 01:14:23,463
Being the One is just
like being in love.

807
01:14:24,100 --> 01:14:27,092
No one can tell you you're in love.
You just know it...

808
01:14:27,269 --> 01:14:28,555
...through and through.

809
01:14:28,729 --> 01:14:30,766
Balls to bones.

810
01:14:33,484 --> 01:14:35,020
Well...

811
01:14:36,112 --> 01:14:38,194
... I'd better have a look at you.

812
01:14:39,573 --> 01:14:41,029
Open your mouth. Say, "Ah."

813
01:14:55,423 --> 01:14:57,084
Okay...

814
01:14:57,717 --> 01:15:02,632
Now I'm supposed to say,
"Hmm, that's interesting, but..."

815
01:15:03,180 --> 01:15:04,386
Then you say...

816
01:15:05,099 --> 01:15:06,305
..."but what?"

817
01:15:06,475 --> 01:15:10,389
But you already know
what I'm going to tell you.

818
01:15:11,814 --> 01:15:14,772
- I'm not the One.
- Sorry, kid.

819
01:15:16,402 --> 01:15:18,393
You got the gift...

820
01:15:19,488 --> 01:15:22,355
...but it looks like
you're waiting for something.

821
01:15:26,746 --> 01:15:30,455
- What?
- Your next life, maybe. Who knows?

822
01:15:31,000 --> 01:15:33,287
That's the way these things go.

823
01:15:34,295 --> 01:15:36,787
- What's funny?
- Morpheus.

824
01:15:40,217 --> 01:15:41,958
He almost had me convinced.

825
01:15:42,178 --> 01:15:43,418
I know.

826
01:15:44,889 --> 01:15:46,971
Poor Morpheus.

827
01:15:49,351 --> 01:15:52,469
Without him, we're lost.

828
01:15:54,065 --> 01:15:56,227
What do you mean, "without him"?

829
01:16:00,154 --> 01:16:02,111
Are you sure
you want to hear this?

830
01:16:04,325 --> 01:16:07,113
Morpheus believes in you, Neo.

831
01:16:08,829 --> 01:16:10,991
And no one, not you, not even me...

832
01:16:11,207 --> 01:16:13,448
...can convince him otherwise.

833
01:16:13,834 --> 01:16:16,246
He believes it so blindly...

834
01:16:16,504 --> 01:16:20,839
...that he's going to sacrifice
his life to save yours.

835
01:16:21,092 --> 01:16:25,006
- What?
- You're going to have to make a choice.

836
01:16:25,679 --> 01:16:29,217
In the one hand,
you'll have Morpheus' life.

837
01:16:29,809 --> 01:16:32,642
And in the other hand,
you'll have your own.

838
01:16:34,105 --> 01:16:36,346
One of you is going to die.

839
01:16:38,484 --> 01:16:41,693
Which one...will be up to you.

840
01:16:43,072 --> 01:16:45,029
I'm sorry, kiddo. I really am.

841
01:16:45,241 --> 01:16:46,948
You have a good soul.

842
01:16:48,035 --> 01:16:50,777
And I hate giving
good people bad news.

843
01:16:53,874 --> 01:16:55,330
Don't worry about it.

844
01:16:55,584 --> 01:16:58,042
As soon as you
step outside that door...

845
01:16:58,295 --> 01:17:00,377
...you'll start feeling better.

846
01:17:01,132 --> 01:17:04,875
You'll remember you don't believe
in any of this fate crap.

847
01:17:05,719 --> 01:17:08,507
You're in control of your own life.

848
01:17:09,306 --> 01:17:10,592
Remember?

849
01:17:12,518 --> 01:17:13,883
Here...

850
01:17:15,354 --> 01:17:16,890
...take a cookie.

851
01:17:17,481 --> 01:17:20,769
I promise, by the time
you're done eating it...

852
01:17:21,735 --> 01:17:24,102
...you'll feel right as rain.

853
01:17:33,289 --> 01:17:34,700
What was said...

854
01:17:35,249 --> 01:17:36,739
...was for you...

855
01:17:37,251 --> 01:17:39,083
...and for you alone.

856
01:18:02,026 --> 01:18:03,232
They're on their way.

857
01:18:33,140 --> 01:18:34,096
What is that?

858
01:18:48,822 --> 01:18:50,187
Whoa, déjà vu.

859
01:18:53,744 --> 01:18:56,532
- What did you just say?
- Nothing. Just had déjà vu.

860
01:18:56,705 --> 01:18:58,446
- What did you see?
- What happened?

861
01:18:59,833 --> 01:19:02,040
A black cat went past us...

862
01:19:02,253 --> 01:19:03,914
...then another just like it.

863
01:19:04,088 --> 01:19:06,420
How much like it?
Was it the same cat?

864
01:19:06,840 --> 01:19:08,456
Might have been. I'm not sure.

865
01:19:08,676 --> 01:19:10,258
Switch, Apoc.

866
01:19:13,931 --> 01:19:16,969
- What is it?
- A déjà vu is usually a glitch in the Matrix.

867
01:19:17,142 --> 01:19:19,429
It happens when they change something.

868
01:19:22,690 --> 01:19:23,680
Oh, my God.

869
01:19:25,693 --> 01:19:27,275
Let's go.

870
01:19:31,699 --> 01:19:33,531
They cut the hard line.
It's a trap! Get out!

871
01:19:39,248 --> 01:19:40,238
Oh, no.

872
01:20:20,497 --> 01:20:23,034
That's what they changed.
We're trapped.

873
01:20:23,250 --> 01:20:25,161
Be calm. Give me your phone.

874
01:20:25,377 --> 01:20:26,867
They'll be able to track it.

875
01:20:27,087 --> 01:20:28,577
We have no choice.

876
01:20:29,965 --> 01:20:31,296
- Operator.
- <i>Tank?</i>

877
01:20:31,467 --> 01:20:34,425
<i>Find a structural drawing
of this building. Find it fast.</i>

878
01:20:42,227 --> 01:20:44,719
- Got it!
- I need <i>the main wet-wall.</i>

879
01:20:48,108 --> 01:20:50,645
Eighth floor.
They're on the eighth floor.

880
01:20:50,944 --> 01:20:52,434
Switch, straight ahead.

881
01:21:00,454 --> 01:21:02,616
I hope the Oracle
gave you some good news.

882
01:21:10,839 --> 01:21:12,421
<i>Now left. That's it.</i>

883
01:21:12,716 --> 01:21:14,081
Good.

884
01:21:23,435 --> 01:21:24,766
Where are they?

885
01:22:25,205 --> 01:22:26,411
They're in the walls.

886
01:22:27,749 --> 01:22:28,989
In the walls!

887
01:22:50,397 --> 01:22:51,853
It's an agent!

888
01:23:01,033 --> 01:23:03,400
You must get Neo out!
He's all that matters!

889
01:23:03,577 --> 01:23:05,693
No! No, Morpheus! Don't!

890
01:23:05,913 --> 01:23:07,403
Trinity, go!

891
01:23:07,581 --> 01:23:08,946
Go!

892
01:23:15,255 --> 01:23:17,166
- We can't leave him!
- We have to!

893
01:23:41,615 --> 01:23:43,276
Cypher, come on!

894
01:23:48,288 --> 01:23:50,529
The great Morpheus.

895
01:23:50,749 --> 01:23:52,035
We meet at last.

896
01:23:52,209 --> 01:23:53,745
And you are?

897
01:23:53,919 --> 01:23:55,626
A Smith.

898
01:23:55,963 --> 01:23:57,249
Agent Smith.

899
01:23:57,798 --> 01:23:59,835
You all look the same to me.

900
01:24:55,522 --> 01:24:56,808
Take him.

901
01:25:03,530 --> 01:25:04,895
No!

902
01:25:10,037 --> 01:25:11,869
- Operator.
- I need <i>an exit, fast.</i>

903
01:25:12,122 --> 01:25:13,783
- <i>Cypher.</i>
- Yeah.

904
01:25:13,957 --> 01:25:16,824
There was an accident.
Goddamn car accident.

905
01:25:17,169 --> 01:25:19,001
<i>All of a sudden, boom.</i>

906
01:25:19,212 --> 01:25:22,455
- Somebody up there still likes me.
- I got you.

907
01:25:22,633 --> 01:25:26,046
- <i>Just get me out of here fast.</i>
- Nearest exit, Franklin and Erie.

908
01:25:26,219 --> 01:25:27,459
An old TV repair shop.

909
01:25:27,638 --> 01:25:28,844
Right.

910
01:25:31,850 --> 01:25:33,466
- Operator.
- <i>Tank, it's me.</i>

911
01:25:33,727 --> 01:25:35,058
Is Morpheus alive?

912
01:25:35,228 --> 01:25:36,468
Is Morpheus alive, Tank?

913
01:25:36,647 --> 01:25:38,979
<i>Yes. They're moving him.
I don't know where to yet.</i>

914
01:25:39,149 --> 01:25:42,562
- He's alive. We need an exit.
- You're not far from Cypher.

915
01:25:42,778 --> 01:25:44,234
- <i>Cypher?</i>
- I know.

916
01:25:44,404 --> 01:25:46,520
- <i>I sent him to Franklin and Erie.</i>
- Got it.

917
01:25:55,582 --> 01:25:56,788
Got him.

918
01:26:07,719 --> 01:26:10,677
- Where are they?
- Making the call.

919
01:26:10,931 --> 01:26:12,137
Good.

920
01:26:25,904 --> 01:26:27,190
You first, Neo.

921
01:26:29,658 --> 01:26:30,944
Shit!

922
01:26:39,584 --> 01:26:41,746
I don't know. It just went dead.

923
01:27:08,488 --> 01:27:09,728
<i>Hello, Trinity.</i>

924
01:27:10,157 --> 01:27:11,443
Cypher? Where's Tank?

925
01:27:17,080 --> 01:27:18,662
You know...

926
01:27:19,833 --> 01:27:21,949
...for a long time...

927
01:27:23,170 --> 01:27:26,037
... I thought I was in love with you.

928
01:27:26,840 --> 01:27:28,877
<i>I used to dream about you.</i>

929
01:27:30,010 --> 01:27:32,752
You're a beautiful woman, Trinity.

930
01:27:32,971 --> 01:27:35,338
<i>Too bad things had
to turn out this way.</i>

931
01:27:36,057 --> 01:27:37,468
You killed them.

932
01:27:37,642 --> 01:27:38,973
- What?
- Oh, God.

933
01:27:39,186 --> 01:27:40,551
I'm tired, Trinity.

934
01:27:42,022 --> 01:27:43,854
I'm tired of this war...

935
01:27:44,191 --> 01:27:46,979
...tired of fighting.
I'm tired of this ship...

936
01:27:47,360 --> 01:27:51,979
...of being cold, of eating
the same goddamn goop every day.

937
01:27:54,493 --> 01:27:55,858
But most of all...

938
01:27:56,036 --> 01:27:59,245
<i>...I'm tired of that jackoff
and all of his bullshit.</i>

939
01:28:00,373 --> 01:28:01,659
Surprise, asshole!

940
01:28:02,209 --> 01:28:04,496
I bet you never saw this coming...

941
01:28:04,711 --> 01:28:05,917
...did you?

942
01:28:08,048 --> 01:28:10,380
God, I wish I could be there...

943
01:28:10,967 --> 01:28:12,503
...when they break you.

944
01:28:13,553 --> 01:28:16,671
I wish I could walk in
just when it happens...

945
01:28:17,390 --> 01:28:19,131
...so right then...

946
01:28:19,351 --> 01:28:20,682
...you'd know it was me.

947
01:28:21,394 --> 01:28:24,056
- You gave them Morpheus.
- He <i>lied to us, Trinity.</i>

948
01:28:24,648 --> 01:28:26,184
He tricked us!

949
01:28:26,691 --> 01:28:28,682
If you had told us the truth...

950
01:28:28,860 --> 01:28:31,898
...we would've told you to shove
that red pill up your ass!

951
01:28:32,072 --> 01:28:34,359
That is not true, Cypher.
He set us free.

952
01:28:34,533 --> 01:28:37,321
"Free." You call this "free"?

953
01:28:39,746 --> 01:28:42,238
All I do is what he tells me to do.

954
01:28:43,875 --> 01:28:46,742
If I got to choose between that
and the Matrix...

955
01:28:47,921 --> 01:28:49,207
... I choose the Matrix.

956
01:28:49,422 --> 01:28:51,038
The Matrix isn't real.

957
01:28:51,341 --> 01:28:52,752
<i>I disagree, Trinity.</i>

958
01:28:52,968 --> 01:28:55,209
I think the Matrix...

959
01:28:55,595 --> 01:28:58,132
...can be more real than this world.

960
01:29:00,350 --> 01:29:02,842
All I do is pull the plug here...

961
01:29:03,228 --> 01:29:04,434
...but there...

962
01:29:04,938 --> 01:29:07,225
<i>...you have to watch Apoc die.</i>

963
01:29:11,945 --> 01:29:13,185
No!

964
01:29:14,990 --> 01:29:17,948
- <i>Welcome to the real world, huh?</i>
- But you're out, Cypher.

965
01:29:18,159 --> 01:29:20,651
- <i>You can't go back.</i>
- No, that's what you think.

966
01:29:20,871 --> 01:29:22,487
<i>They're gonna reinsert my body.</i>

967
01:29:22,664 --> 01:29:26,282
<i>I go back to sleep. When I wake up,
I won't remember a goddamn thing.</i>

968
01:29:26,501 --> 01:29:30,711
By the way, if you have anything
terribly important to say to Switch...

969
01:29:31,006 --> 01:29:33,498
- <i>...I suggest you say it now.</i>
- No, please don't.

970
01:29:33,967 --> 01:29:35,583
Not like this.

971
01:29:37,304 --> 01:29:38,920
Not like this.

972
01:29:43,310 --> 01:29:44,550
Too late.

973
01:29:45,186 --> 01:29:46,551
Goddamn you, Cypher!

974
01:29:46,730 --> 01:29:48,641
Don't hate me, Trinity.

975
01:29:48,982 --> 01:29:50,893
I'm just a messenger.

976
01:29:51,276 --> 01:29:54,439
And right now,
I'm going to prove it to you.

977
01:29:55,530 --> 01:29:57,191
If Morpheus was right...

978
01:29:57,657 --> 01:29:59,648
...there's no way
I can pull this plug.

979
01:30:00,243 --> 01:30:01,699
<i>I mean, if Neo's the One...</i>

980
01:30:02,203 --> 01:30:04,069
<i>...then there'd have to be...</i>

981
01:30:04,289 --> 01:30:06,906
...some kind of a miracle to stop me.

982
01:30:07,417 --> 01:30:08,748
Right?

983
01:30:08,919 --> 01:30:12,287
I mean, how can he be the One
if he's dead?

984
01:30:13,632 --> 01:30:15,839
<i>You never did answer me before...</i>

985
01:30:16,176 --> 01:30:18,508
<i>...if you bought into
Morpheus' bullshit.</i>

986
01:30:18,845 --> 01:30:22,054
Come on. All I want
is a little yes or no.

987
01:30:23,433 --> 01:30:25,800
Look into his eyes...

988
01:30:26,519 --> 01:30:27,975
<i>...those big, pretty eyes...</i>

989
01:30:30,732 --> 01:30:32,097
...and tell me...

990
01:30:32,817 --> 01:30:34,057
<i>...yes...</i>

991
01:30:34,444 --> 01:30:35,809
<i>...or no.</i>

992
01:30:37,030 --> 01:30:38,646
- Yes.
- <i>No.</i>

993
01:30:39,032 --> 01:30:40,739
I don't believe it.

994
01:30:41,368 --> 01:30:46,158
Believe it or not, you piece of shit,
you're still going to burn!

995
01:31:04,641 --> 01:31:05,847
You first.

996
01:31:14,025 --> 01:31:16,266
- You're hurt.
- I'll be all right.

997
01:31:19,072 --> 01:31:20,312
Dozer?

998
01:31:38,466 --> 01:31:40,878
Have you ever stood and stared at it?

999
01:31:41,761 --> 01:31:44,879
Marveled at its beauty...

1000
01:31:45,265 --> 01:31:47,552
...its genius?

1001
01:31:48,727 --> 01:31:50,593
Billions of people...

1002
01:31:50,812 --> 01:31:53,554
...just living out their lives...

1003
01:31:54,607 --> 01:31:56,268
...oblivious.

1004
01:32:00,864 --> 01:32:03,777
Did you know that the first Matrix...

1005
01:32:03,992 --> 01:32:08,657
...was designed to be a perfect
human world where none suffered...

1006
01:32:09,205 --> 01:32:12,072
...where everyone would be happy.

1007
01:32:12,625 --> 01:32:14,161
It was a disaster.

1008
01:32:14,377 --> 01:32:18,746
No one would accept the program.
Entire crops were lost.

1009
01:32:19,591 --> 01:32:21,377
Some believe that...

1010
01:32:21,593 --> 01:32:26,008
...we lacked the programming language
to describe your perfect world.

1011
01:32:26,222 --> 01:32:29,135
But I believe that, as a species...

1012
01:32:29,392 --> 01:32:33,226
...human beings define
their reality through misery...

1013
01:32:33,480 --> 01:32:34,811
...and suffering.

1014
01:32:35,065 --> 01:32:37,773
So the perfect world was a dream...

1015
01:32:37,984 --> 01:32:42,854
...that your primitive cerebrum
kept trying to wake up from.

1016
01:32:44,157 --> 01:32:47,900
Which is why the Matrix was
redesigned to this.

1017
01:32:48,328 --> 01:32:51,491
The peak of your civilization.

1018
01:32:51,706 --> 01:32:54,073
I say "your civilization"...

1019
01:32:54,292 --> 01:32:58,957
...because as soon as we started thinking
for you, it really became our civilization...

1020
01:32:59,130 --> 01:33:01,747
...which is, of course,
what this is all about.

1021
01:33:03,093 --> 01:33:05,630
Evolution, Morpheus.

1022
01:33:05,970 --> 01:33:07,256
Evolution.

1023
01:33:09,516 --> 01:33:11,382
Like the dinosaur.

1024
01:33:13,561 --> 01:33:15,222
Look out that window.

1025
01:33:15,980 --> 01:33:18,062
You had your time.

1026
01:33:18,775 --> 01:33:22,689
The future is our world, Morpheus.

1027
01:33:23,029 --> 01:33:25,441
The future is our time.

1028
01:33:29,536 --> 01:33:30,867
There could be a problem.

1029
01:33:31,746 --> 01:33:34,955
- What are they doing to him?
- They're breaking into his mind.

1030
01:33:35,125 --> 01:33:37,583
It's like hacking a computer.
All it takes is time.

1031
01:33:37,794 --> 01:33:39,000
How much time?

1032
01:33:39,295 --> 01:33:42,413
Depends on the mind.
But eventually, it'll crack...

1033
01:33:42,632 --> 01:33:47,126
...and his alpha patterns
will change from this to this.

1034
01:33:47,345 --> 01:33:50,303
When it does, he'll tell them
anything they want to know.

1035
01:33:50,515 --> 01:33:51,755
What do they want?

1036
01:33:51,933 --> 01:33:55,892
The leader of every ship is given codes
to Zion's mainframe computer.

1037
01:33:56,062 --> 01:33:59,145
If an agent got the codes
and got into Zion's mainframe...

1038
01:33:59,315 --> 01:34:02,353
...they could destroy us.
We can't let that happen.

1039
01:34:02,527 --> 01:34:06,145
Trinity, Zion's more important
than me or you...

1040
01:34:06,322 --> 01:34:07,528
...or even Morpheus.

1041
01:34:11,411 --> 01:34:15,450
- There has to be something that we can do.
- There is. We pull the plug.

1042
01:34:18,585 --> 01:34:20,326
You're going to kill him?

1043
01:34:20,503 --> 01:34:21,709
Kill Morpheus?

1044
01:34:22,297 --> 01:34:24,004
We don't have any other choice.

1045
01:34:30,763 --> 01:34:33,721
Never send a human
to do a machine's job.

1046
01:34:33,933 --> 01:34:35,799
If indeed the insider has failed...

1047
01:34:35,977 --> 01:34:39,220
...they'll sever the connection
as soon as possible, unless--

1048
01:34:39,439 --> 01:34:41,146
They're dead. In either case--

1049
01:34:41,316 --> 01:34:44,900
We have no choice, but to continue
as planned. Deploy the sentinels.

1050
01:34:45,069 --> 01:34:46,275
Immediately.

1051
01:34:51,451 --> 01:34:54,159
Morpheus, you were more
than a leader to us.

1052
01:34:55,121 --> 01:34:57,362
You were a father.

1053
01:34:58,833 --> 01:35:00,790
We'll miss you always.

1054
01:35:07,884 --> 01:35:09,090
Stop!

1055
01:35:09,886 --> 01:35:11,468
I don't believe this is happening.

1056
01:35:11,638 --> 01:35:13,629
- Neo, this has to be done.
- Does it?

1057
01:35:14,432 --> 01:35:15,888
I don't know.

1058
01:35:16,059 --> 01:35:19,268
- This can't be just coincidence.
- What are you talking about?

1059
01:35:19,437 --> 01:35:22,099
The Oracle...
She told me this would happen.

1060
01:35:22,523 --> 01:35:26,687
She told me that I would
have to make a choice.

1061
01:35:27,153 --> 01:35:28,359
What choice?

1062
01:35:31,908 --> 01:35:33,945
- What are you doing?
- I'm going in.

1063
01:35:34,118 --> 01:35:36,576
- No, you're not.
- I have to.

1064
01:35:36,788 --> 01:35:40,577
Neo, Morpheus sacrificed himself
so that we could get you out.

1065
01:35:40,750 --> 01:35:43,117
There is no way
that you're going back in.

1066
01:35:43,294 --> 01:35:47,162
Morpheus did what he did because
he believed I'm something I'm not.

1067
01:35:48,258 --> 01:35:49,464
What?

1068
01:35:49,676 --> 01:35:51,292
I'm not the One, Trinity.

1069
01:35:51,678 --> 01:35:54,636
- The Oracle hit me with that too.
- No, you have to be.

1070
01:35:54,847 --> 01:35:57,509
I'm sorry, I'm not.
I'm just another guy.

1071
01:35:58,184 --> 01:35:59,515
No, Neo, that's not true.

1072
01:36:00,019 --> 01:36:02,681
- It can't be true.
- Why?

1073
01:36:06,317 --> 01:36:10,481
Neo, this is loco. They've got Morpheus
in a military-controlled building.

1074
01:36:10,697 --> 01:36:15,032
Even if you somehow got inside, those
are agents holding him. Three of them.

1075
01:36:16,369 --> 01:36:20,237
I want Morpheus back too,
but what you're talking about is suicide.

1076
01:36:20,456 --> 01:36:23,369
I know that's what it looks like,
but it's not.

1077
01:36:23,543 --> 01:36:25,955
I can't explain to you why it's not.

1078
01:36:27,046 --> 01:36:30,789
Morpheus believed something,
and he was ready to give his life for it.

1079
01:36:31,009 --> 01:36:34,127
I understand that now.
That's why I have to go.

1080
01:36:34,304 --> 01:36:36,796
- Why?
- Because I believe in something.

1081
01:36:37,265 --> 01:36:38,505
What?

1082
01:36:39,267 --> 01:36:40,974
I believe I can bring him back.

1083
01:36:57,994 --> 01:36:59,905
- What are you doing?
- Going with you.

1084
01:37:00,330 --> 01:37:02,241
- No, you're not.
- "No"?

1085
01:37:03,374 --> 01:37:05,490
Let me tell you what I believe.

1086
01:37:05,918 --> 01:37:08,330
Morpheus means more to me
than he does to you.

1087
01:37:08,713 --> 01:37:13,002
I believe if you are really serious about
saving him, you will need my help.

1088
01:37:13,217 --> 01:37:15,333
And since I am the ranking officer...

1089
01:37:15,553 --> 01:37:18,386
...if you don't like it,
I believe you can go to hell.

1090
01:37:19,182 --> 01:37:21,549
Because you aren't going anywhere else.

1091
01:37:22,018 --> 01:37:24,760
Tank, load us up.

1092
01:37:34,447 --> 01:37:37,781
I'd like to share a revelation
that I've had...

1093
01:37:38,117 --> 01:37:39,733
...during my time here.

1094
01:37:39,952 --> 01:37:44,037
It came to me when I tried
to classify your species...

1095
01:37:44,248 --> 01:37:46,489
...and I realized...

1096
01:37:46,709 --> 01:37:48,996
...that you're not actually mammals.

1097
01:37:51,214 --> 01:37:53,672
Every mammal on this planet...

1098
01:37:54,050 --> 01:37:56,883
...instinctively develops
a natural equilibrium...

1099
01:37:57,053 --> 01:37:58,964
...with the surrounding environment.

1100
01:37:59,138 --> 01:38:01,049
But you humans do not.

1101
01:38:01,599 --> 01:38:05,137
You move to an area,
and you multiply...

1102
01:38:05,395 --> 01:38:09,810
...and multiply, until every
natural resource is consumed.

1103
01:38:10,191 --> 01:38:12,273
The only way you can survive...

1104
01:38:12,527 --> 01:38:15,565
...is to spread to another area.

1105
01:38:20,952 --> 01:38:23,819
There is another organism
on this planet...

1106
01:38:24,038 --> 01:38:26,075
...that follows the same pattern.

1107
01:38:26,666 --> 01:38:28,282
Do you know what it is?

1108
01:38:28,751 --> 01:38:30,492
A virus.

1109
01:38:31,838 --> 01:38:34,956
Human beings are a disease.

1110
01:38:35,341 --> 01:38:36,923
A cancer of this planet.

1111
01:38:37,135 --> 01:38:39,251
You are a plague.

1112
01:38:39,762 --> 01:38:41,173
And we...

1113
01:38:41,347 --> 01:38:42,758
...are the cure.

1114
01:38:43,724 --> 01:38:45,135
Okay, so what do you need?

1115
01:38:45,726 --> 01:38:46,966
Besides a miracle.

1116
01:38:47,478 --> 01:38:48,684
Guns.

1117
01:38:49,564 --> 01:38:50,804
Lots of guns.

1118
01:39:03,661 --> 01:39:06,073
No one has ever done
anything like this.

1119
01:39:07,373 --> 01:39:09,205
That's why it's going to work.

1120
01:39:13,379 --> 01:39:15,245
Why isn't the serum working?

1121
01:39:15,882 --> 01:39:18,214
Perhaps we're asking
the wrong questions.

1122
01:39:20,303 --> 01:39:21,509
Leave me with him.

1123
01:39:24,140 --> 01:39:25,346
Now.

1124
01:39:36,444 --> 01:39:38,026
Hold on, Morpheus.

1125
01:39:38,237 --> 01:39:41,025
They're coming for you.
They're coming.

1126
01:39:43,409 --> 01:39:45,525
Can you hear me, Morpheus?

1127
01:39:45,745 --> 01:39:48,407
I'm going to be honest...

1128
01:39:48,789 --> 01:39:50,029
...with you.

1129
01:39:54,420 --> 01:39:55,751
I...

1130
01:39:56,881 --> 01:39:59,964
...hate this place...

1131
01:40:00,384 --> 01:40:02,671
...this zoo...

1132
01:40:02,929 --> 01:40:04,169
...this prison...

1133
01:40:04,347 --> 01:40:07,465
...this reality,
whatever you want to call it.

1134
01:40:07,683 --> 01:40:09,970
I can't stand it any longer.

1135
01:40:10,770 --> 01:40:12,602
It's the smell.

1136
01:40:13,940 --> 01:40:15,851
If there is such a thing.

1137
01:40:16,234 --> 01:40:19,522
I feel saturated by it.

1138
01:40:20,947 --> 01:40:22,563
I can...

1139
01:40:22,782 --> 01:40:24,147
...taste...

1140
01:40:24,325 --> 01:40:26,316
...your stink.

1141
01:40:26,536 --> 01:40:30,279
And every time I do, I fear that
I have somehow been infected by it.

1142
01:40:30,498 --> 01:40:32,080
It's repulsive.

1143
01:40:32,291 --> 01:40:33,747
Isn't it?

1144
01:40:35,920 --> 01:40:38,207
I must get out of here.

1145
01:40:38,589 --> 01:40:40,876
I must get free.

1146
01:40:41,092 --> 01:40:43,959
And in this mind is the key.

1147
01:40:44,220 --> 01:40:45,802
My key.

1148
01:40:45,972 --> 01:40:49,010
Once Zion is destroyed,
there is no need for me to be here.

1149
01:40:49,225 --> 01:40:50,841
Do you understand?

1150
01:40:51,143 --> 01:40:52,554
I need the codes.

1151
01:40:52,812 --> 01:40:55,144
I have to get inside Zion...

1152
01:40:55,439 --> 01:40:57,931
...and you have to tell me how.

1153
01:40:58,317 --> 01:41:00,274
You're going to tell me...

1154
01:41:00,486 --> 01:41:02,602
...or you're going to die.

1155
01:41:22,842 --> 01:41:25,379
Please remove any metallic items
you're carrying.

1156
01:41:25,595 --> 01:41:26,926
Keys, loose change.

1157
01:41:29,807 --> 01:41:31,013
Holy shit!

1158
01:41:43,029 --> 01:41:45,771
Backup. Send backup.

1159
01:42:09,805 --> 01:42:11,421
Freeze!

1160
01:44:25,775 --> 01:44:27,482
What were you doing?

1161
01:44:28,569 --> 01:44:29,900
He doesn't know.

1162
01:44:30,112 --> 01:44:31,602
Know what?

1163
01:44:59,725 --> 01:45:02,183
I think they're trying to save him.

1164
01:45:17,034 --> 01:45:18,775
There is no spoon.

1165
01:45:48,440 --> 01:45:50,556
Find them and destroy them!

1166
01:45:52,236 --> 01:45:54,102
I repeat, we are under attack!

1167
01:46:28,147 --> 01:46:29,637
Help!

1168
01:46:50,920 --> 01:46:52,126
Only human.

1169
01:46:53,255 --> 01:46:54,916
Dodge this.

1170
01:47:07,394 --> 01:47:08,930
- How did you do that?
- Do what?

1171
01:47:09,355 --> 01:47:13,223
You moved like they do.
I've never seen anyone move that fast.

1172
01:47:14,360 --> 01:47:15,771
It wasn't fast enough.

1173
01:47:18,489 --> 01:47:19,820
Can you fly that thing?

1174
01:47:21,200 --> 01:47:22,656
Not yet.

1175
01:47:25,329 --> 01:47:27,195
- Operator.
- I need <i>a pilot program...</i>

1176
01:47:27,373 --> 01:47:29,614
<i>...for a B-212 helicopter.</i>

1177
01:47:30,125 --> 01:47:31,365
<i>Hurry.</i>

1178
01:47:39,343 --> 01:47:40,925
Let's go.

1179
01:47:55,943 --> 01:47:57,183
No.

1180
01:48:48,704 --> 01:48:51,366
Morpheus, get up.
Get up, get up.

1181
01:49:29,369 --> 01:49:31,155
He's not going to make it.

1182
01:49:40,214 --> 01:49:41,670
I got you.

1183
01:51:30,157 --> 01:51:31,613
I knew it.

1184
01:51:32,284 --> 01:51:33,490
He's the One.

1185
01:51:49,343 --> 01:51:51,584
Do you believe it now, Trinity?

1186
01:51:57,559 --> 01:51:59,095
The Oracle...

1187
01:51:59,645 --> 01:52:01,977
- She told me--
- She told you...

1188
01:52:02,439 --> 01:52:05,602
...exactly what you needed to hear.
That's all.

1189
01:52:06,652 --> 01:52:09,644
Neo, sooner or later you'll realize,
just as I did...

1190
01:52:09,947 --> 01:52:12,860
...there's a difference
between knowing the path...

1191
01:52:13,033 --> 01:52:14,319
...and walking the path.

1192
01:52:17,329 --> 01:52:19,195
- Operator.
- <i>Tank.</i>

1193
01:52:19,373 --> 01:52:22,115
- It's good to hear your voice, sir.
- We need <i>an exit.</i>

1194
01:52:22,334 --> 01:52:25,076
Got one ready. Subway station,
State and Balboa.

1195
01:52:38,016 --> 01:52:40,553
- Damn it!
- The trace was completed.

1196
01:52:40,769 --> 01:52:44,637
- We have their position.
- Sentinels are standing by.

1197
01:52:46,066 --> 01:52:47,602
Order the strike.

1198
01:52:54,074 --> 01:52:56,111
They're not out yet.

1199
01:53:07,254 --> 01:53:08,619
You first, Morpheus.

1200
01:53:29,318 --> 01:53:31,605
Neo, I want to tell you something...

1201
01:53:34,865 --> 01:53:38,824
...but I'm afraid of
what it could mean if I do.

1202
01:53:42,414 --> 01:53:45,748
Everything the Oracle
told me has come true.

1203
01:53:48,503 --> 01:53:49,993
Everything but this.

1204
01:53:51,882 --> 01:53:53,338
But what?

1205
01:54:18,784 --> 01:54:20,570
- What the hell happened?
- An agent.

1206
01:54:20,786 --> 01:54:22,652
- You have to send me back.
- I can't.

1207
01:54:24,664 --> 01:54:26,655
Mr. Anderson.

1208
01:54:28,835 --> 01:54:30,291
Run, Neo. Run.

1209
01:54:35,592 --> 01:54:38,710
- What is he doing?
- He's beginning to believe.

1210
01:55:05,664 --> 01:55:07,075
You're empty.

1211
01:55:07,624 --> 01:55:08,955
So are you.

1212
01:55:42,075 --> 01:55:45,067
I'm going to enjoy watching you die...

1213
01:55:46,037 --> 01:55:47,277
...Mr. Anderson.

1214
01:56:28,246 --> 01:56:30,283
Jesus, he's killing him.

1215
01:57:56,459 --> 01:57:58,621
You hear that, Mr. Anderson?

1216
01:57:59,337 --> 01:58:02,295
That is the sound of inevitability.

1217
01:58:04,968 --> 01:58:08,302
It is the sound of your death.

1218
01:58:09,180 --> 01:58:11,512
Goodbye, Mr. Anderson.

1219
01:58:11,725 --> 01:58:13,432
My name...

1220
01:58:16,354 --> 01:58:18,436
...is Neo.

1221
01:58:50,722 --> 01:58:52,838
- What happened?
- I don't know. I lost him.

1222
01:58:55,268 --> 01:58:56,508
Oh, shit.

1223
01:59:08,865 --> 01:59:10,230
Sentinels.

1224
01:59:11,076 --> 01:59:13,283
- How long?
- Five, maybe six minutes.

1225
01:59:15,330 --> 01:59:17,492
Tank, charge the EMP.

1226
01:59:17,749 --> 01:59:21,834
- We can't use that until he's out.
- I know, Trinity. Don't worry.

1227
01:59:22,003 --> 01:59:23,084
He's gonna make it.

1228
01:59:23,254 --> 01:59:25,165
Flat or pumps? No, just--

1229
01:59:25,423 --> 01:59:28,336
What the shit? That's my phone!

1230
01:59:28,760 --> 01:59:30,342
That guy took my phone!

1231
01:59:32,847 --> 01:59:34,963
Got him! He's on the run.

1232
01:59:35,141 --> 01:59:37,929
Mr. Wizard, get me the hell out of here!

1233
01:59:38,144 --> 01:59:40,055
<i>I got an old exit.
Wabash and Lake.</i>

1234
01:59:43,983 --> 01:59:44,973
Oh, shit!

1235
02:00:06,548 --> 02:00:08,539
Help! Need a little help!

1236
02:00:10,176 --> 02:00:11,416
<i>The door.</i>

1237
02:00:27,402 --> 02:00:28,858
<i>The door on your left.</i>

1238
02:00:29,779 --> 02:00:31,065
<i>No, your other left!</i>

1239
02:00:37,746 --> 02:00:39,282
<i>The back door.</i>

1240
02:00:59,684 --> 02:01:00,924
Oh, no.

1241
02:01:02,562 --> 02:01:04,098
Here they come.

1242
02:01:32,884 --> 02:01:34,090
He's going to make it.

1243
02:01:44,354 --> 02:01:47,437
<i>The fire escape at the end
of the alley, room 303.</i>

1244
02:02:22,684 --> 02:02:24,391
They're inside.

1245
02:02:25,979 --> 02:02:26,969
Hurry, Neo.

1246
02:03:23,202 --> 02:03:24,442
It can't be.

1247
02:03:32,170 --> 02:03:33,535
Check him.

1248
02:03:37,592 --> 02:03:39,082
He's gone.

1249
02:03:45,850 --> 02:03:48,262
Goodbye, Mr. Anderson.

1250
02:03:58,363 --> 02:04:00,320
I'm not afraid anymore.

1251
02:04:01,908 --> 02:04:06,197
The Oracle told me that I would
fall in love, and that that man...

1252
02:04:06,746 --> 02:04:08,862
...the man that I loved
would be the One.

1253
02:04:12,001 --> 02:04:13,912
So you see...

1254
02:04:14,629 --> 02:04:16,620
...you can't be dead.

1255
02:04:18,216 --> 02:04:20,048
You can't be...

1256
02:04:21,594 --> 02:04:23,756
...because I love you.

1257
02:04:25,640 --> 02:04:27,301
You hear me?

1258
02:04:28,434 --> 02:04:30,095
I love you.

1259
02:04:53,918 --> 02:04:55,158
Now, get up.

1260
02:05:04,053 --> 02:05:05,043
No.

1261
02:05:31,581 --> 02:05:32,787
How?

1262
02:05:33,499 --> 02:05:34,739
He is the One.

1263
02:07:59,187 --> 02:08:00,803
<i>I know you're out there.</i>

1264
02:08:01,105 --> 02:08:02,937
<i>I can feel you now.</i>

1265
02:08:03,399 --> 02:08:05,185
<i>I know that you're afraid.</i>

1266
02:08:05,443 --> 02:08:06,979
<i>You're afraid of us.</i>

1267
02:08:07,361 --> 02:08:09,147
<i>You're afraid of change.</i>

1268
02:08:10,531 --> 02:08:11,771
<i>I don't know the future.</i>

1269
02:08:11,949 --> 02:08:14,907
<i>I didn't come here to tell you
how this is going to end.</i>

1270
02:08:15,077 --> 02:08:17,944
<i>I came here to tell you
how it's going to begin.</i>

1271
02:08:18,664 --> 02:08:20,371
<i>I'm going to hang up this phone.</i>

1272
02:08:20,541 --> 02:08:23,909
<i>And then I'll show these people
what you don't want them to see.</i>

1273
02:08:24,086 --> 02:08:25,952
<i>I'm going to show them a world...</i>

1274
02:08:26,130 --> 02:08:27,916
<i>...without you.</i>

1275
02:08:28,216 --> 02:08:31,880
<i>A world without rules and controls,
without borders or boundaries.</i>

1276
02:08:32,094 --> 02:08:35,803
